hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","574 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Buhlul ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Abu Bakr and Umar used to walk in front of the funeral, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, used to walk behind it, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about that, and he said: They both know as I know, but they preferred to make it easy for the people. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Isma'il, from Qays, except Buhlul ibn Ubayd."
"602","575 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, and from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, and Abu Maryam, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Whenever I asked I was given, and when I stayed silent I was given first. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari. And we do not know of anyone narrating it from Isma'il, from Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except Ali ibn Abis, and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Yusuf."
"603","576 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: I was informed from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and commanded me that I should not pass by any grave except that I level it."
"604","And from what Zayd ibn Wahb narrated from Ali. 577 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us. 578 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Wahb, and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah informed me, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted me a sira cloak, so I wore it and I saw anger on his face, so I divided it among my womenfolk. And this hadith has been narrated from Ali through various channels, and we do not know of anyone narrating it from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah."
"605","579 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood by the people of al-Nahr, and said: Whatever you hear me narrating to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then hold me to it; and whatever you hear me narrating in other than that, then war is deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed there will be at the end of time a people, young in teeth, foolish in minds, passing out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game, then never returning to it; wherever you meet them, kill them, for killing them is a reward on the Day of Resurrection, and I do not see them but these. Then he advanced toward them. And this hadith has been narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, through other than this channel with wording differing from this wording, so we mentioned each hadith in its place with its wording."
"606","580 - Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Qays al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: It has been mentioned to me that an outcomer will emerge toward the east, so he marched until he reached them, then a man from the Khawarij said: Do not speak to them, then a man from the companions of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Cut off the bridges. He said: So he killed twelve or thirteen, then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Seek for me Dhu al-Thudayyah, so he was sought and not found, and he began to sweat on a cold day, and said: Bring me the grey mule of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he rode it until he reached a depression in the ground, and said: Turn over, and the first to come out, he said: By Allah I have neither lied nor been lied to; and were it not that I fear, I would have informed you of what Allah decreed for you upon his tongue, meaning: his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and people in Yemen witnessed it who said: O Commander of the Faithful, how? He said: Their inclination was with us."
"607","581 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed me, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Wahb informed me: that he was in the army that was with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who marched to the Khawarij, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A people from my ummah will emerge reciting the Quran; your recitation is nothing compared to their recitation, nor your prayer compared to their prayer, nor your fasting compared to their fasting; they recite the Quran, their prayer not passing beyond their throats; they pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game. If the army that strikes them knew what has been decreed for them upon the tongue of their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they would slacken from deeds. And the sign of that is that among them is a man with an upper arm and no forearm, upon his upper arm like the nipple of a woman's breast, upon it white hairs. So you go to Mu'awiyah and the people of Sham and leave these who will succeed you in your offspring and your wealth? By Allah I hope these are those people, for they have shed sacred blood and raided people's pastures, so march in the name of Allah. When we met, and over the Khawarij that day was Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Rasibi, he said to them: Throw down the spears and unsheathe your swords from their scabbards, for I fear they will adjure you as they adjured you on the day of Harura. He said: So they unsheathed the swords and the rest of the people fenced with their spears, then some of them advanced on others, and none of the people was struck that day except two men. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Seek among them the Mukhdaj. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, himself stood and sought him and found him, and said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Then Abidah stood to him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, by Allah besides whom there is no god, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, I indeed heard this hadith, until he made him swear three times while he swore to him."
"608","And from what Muslim al-Batin narrated from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Ali. 582 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Isma'il al-Hanafi, from Muslim al-Batin, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that he took his hand and we set out walking until we reached the bank of the Euphrates, then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no breathed soul except that misery or happiness has preceded for it from Allah. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is deeds for? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated to what he was created for: {As for he who gives and fears, and believes in the best, We will facilitate him to ease; and as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best} the verse. And this hadith has been narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from another channel with close to this wording, and we do not know of Muslim al-Batin narrating, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except this hadith."
"609","And from what Sa'd ibn Ubaydah narrated from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Ali. 583 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, and al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was at a funeral, so he took a stick and began tapping in the ground, then said: There is none among you except that his seat from the Fire or his seat from Paradise has been written. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we then rely? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated: {As for he who gives and fears, and believes in the best, We will facilitate him to ease; and as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best, We will facilitate him to hardship}. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one, from Mansur, and more than one from al-A'mash, and we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"610","584 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"611","585 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man from the Ansar over an expedition, and commanded them to obey him; when he went out he found something against them, so he said: Has not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded you to obey me? They said: Yes. He said: Then gather firewood. So they gathered firewood, then he called for fire and kindled it in the wood, then said: I adjure you, you shall surely enter it. So the people intended that, then a young man from the youngest of them said to them: Do not hasten to enter the Fire; you only fled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the Fire, until you come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if he commands you to enter, then enter. So they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Had you entered it, you would never have come out of it. And this speech is only narrated from Abu Hurayrah, while the isnad of the hadith of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, is a sound isnad."
"612","586 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: No obedience in disobedience to Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"613","587 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are particular with Quraysh and leave us? He said: And is there anything with you? I said: Yes, the daughter of Hamzah. He said: She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. And this hadith has been narrated from Ali through more than one channel. And this isnad is sound, so we sufficed with it."
"614","588 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day sitting with a stick in his hand tapping with it, then he raised his head and said: There is no soul among you except that its station from Paradise and the Fire has been known. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we then rely and not act? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated to what he was created for. Then he recited: {As for he who gives and fears, and believes in the best} to His saying: {And as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best, We will facilitate him to hardship}."
"615","589 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and put a man in command over them, and commanded them to obey him; so he kindled a fire and said: Enter it. So some people wanted to enter it, and others said: We only fled from it, so we will not enter it. So that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to those who wanted to enter it: Had they entered it, they would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection; and he said to the others who refused a good word, and said: No obedience in disobedience to Allah the Mighty and Majestic; obedience is only in what is good."
"616","590 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us. [Truncated in source: sermon text not present in this row; isnad only continues in next row.]"
"617","591 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: O people, establish the hadd punishments upon your slaves, those of them who are married and those who are not married; for a slave-girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed zina, so he commanded me to flog her, so I came to her and she was recently delivered of childbirth, so I feared that if I flogged her she would die, so I mentioned that to him, meaning: to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: You did well. And we do not know of al-Suddi narrating, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except two hadiths, this is one of them, and the other was narrated by al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid, from al-Suddi."
"618","592 - Hatim ibn al-Layth narrated it to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This old man has died. So he said: Go and bury him, and do not innovate anything. He said: So I buried him, then I came to him, so he said: Go and bathe, and do not innovate until you come to me. So I bathed, then I came to him, so he supplicated for me with supplications, nothing being more pleasing to me than having red and black camels in exchange for them. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from al-Suddi except from this channel."
"619","593 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Amir al-Tha'labi, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in marfu' form: {And you make your provision that you deny}, he said: Your gratitude, you saying: We were rained upon by such-and-such star, and by such-and-such star. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Abd al-Rahman except Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, and it is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except from this channel."
"620","594 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in marfu' form, he said: Whoever lies about his dream will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection with tying a grain of barley. And it has been narrated from Ibn Abbas also. And the hadith of Ali is better in isnad, along with his eminence."
"621","595 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever lies about his dream will be burdened with tying a grain of barley on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except from this channel with this isnad."
"622","596 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us. 597 - And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: I entered upon Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, and he had prayed Fajr, while he was sitting in the mosque, so I said to him: If you stood, meaning: to your bed, it would be softer for you. So he said: I heard Ali saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays Fajr, then sits in his prayer place, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their blessing upon him is: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him; and whoever awaits the prayer, the angels invoke blessings upon him, and their blessing upon him is: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him. And it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Abu Hurayrah, and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and a group, so we mentioned it from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and sufficed with it. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel, and Abu Ahmad narrated it, from Isra'il, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"623","598 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Dashtaki narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf made food for us, so he invited us, and we ate and drank wine; when the wine took effect in us, and prayer came, they commanded a man, so he led them in prayer, and he recited: {Say, O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship}, but: we worship what you worship, meaning: so he mixed up in his recitation, so Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say}. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with connected isnad except from the hadith of Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, and that was only before wine was prohibited, then it was prohibited because of that."
"624","599 - Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the hadith of Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abdullah in musnad form except from the hadith of Ubayd ibn Amr. And Ubayd ibn Amr is a man from the people of Basra, weak in hadith."
"625","600 - Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sharik. 601 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated it to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, from Sharik, from Jabir, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to fast Ashura."
"626","602 - And Shu'ayb ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Ashura. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"627","603 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrating from Fudayl ibn Sulayman, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he commanded the siwak, and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant uses the siwak, then stands to pray, the angel stands behind him and listens to his recitation, then draws near him, or a word like it, until he places his mouth upon his mouth, so nothing comes out of his mouth of the Quran except that it enters the belly of the angel; so purify your mouths for the Quran. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with an isnad better than this isnad. And more than one has narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, as mawquf."
"628","And from what Alqamah ibn Qays narrated from Ali. 604 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hakim ibn Jubayr saying: I heard Ibrahim saying: I heard Alqamah saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I was commanded to fight the Nakithin, and the Qasitin, and the Mariqin. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except Hakim ibn Jubayr, and Hakim is not strong, though al-A'mash, and al-Thawri, and others narrated from him."
"629","605 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from Hunayf al-Mu'adhdhin, from Abu al-Ruqqad, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me in the illness in which he died: Give people permission to come to me. So I gave permission, then he said: May Allah curse a people who took the graves of their Prophets as mosques. Then he fainted, and when he recovered, he said: O Ali, give people permission to come to me. So I gave people permission to come to him, then he said: May Allah curse a people who took the graves of their Prophets as a mosque. He said it three times in his illness. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Jarir, from Hunayf al-Mu'adhdhin, from Abu al-Ruqqad, from Alqamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and we do not know of an isnad for it other than this isnad, and we do not know of anyone narrating from Hunayf except Jarir, nor from Abu al-Ruqqad except Hunayf."
"630","And from what Mujahid narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali. 606 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said to us: Shall I not teach you something you say at your sleeping place? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Glorify Allah thirty-three times, and praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times, for a thousand good deeds will be written for you thereby."
"631","607 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Nur ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"632","608 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, and Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his sacrificial animals with him, and commanded him to give in charity their meat, and their skins, and their coverings. And we do not know of Ayyub narrating from Ibn Abi Najih any musnad hadith except this hadith, and this hadith has been narrated from Abd al-Karim by Sufyan al-Thawri, and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and Ibn Jurayj."
"633","609 - As for the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand over his sacrificial camels, and to give in charity their skins and their coverings, and not to give the butcher anything from them."
"634","610 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand over his sacrificial camels, and to divide their skins and their coverings, and commanded me not to give the butcher anything, meaning: from them. And he said: We give him from ourselves."
"635","611 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me: that Mujahid informed him, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed him: that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, informed him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to stand over his sacrificial camels. Then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah."
"636","612 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me: that Mujahid informed him from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla: that he informed him that Ali ibn Abi Talib informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to stand over his sacrificial camels, and commanded him to divide all of them, their meat, and their skins and their coverings, among the poor, and not to give anything for their slaughtering. He said: I said: Did he name for you among whom he divided it? He said: No."
"637","613 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us. 614 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sayf, meaning Ibn Sulayman, he said: I heard Mujahid saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed me, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me concerning his sacrificial camels, so I divided their meat, then he commanded me, so I divided their skins, then he commanded me, so I divided their coverings."
"638","615 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim, and Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand over his sacrificial camels, and commanded me to divide their skins, and their coverings."
"639","616 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand over his sacrificial camels, and to give in charity their skins, and their coverings, and commanded me not to give the butcher anything from them. And we do not know of anyone narrating the hadith of Shu'bah, from Ibn Abi Najih, except Abu Bahr, from Shu'bah."
"640","617 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr, and he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered in his Hajj one hundred camels, among them a camel of Abu Jahl with a gold nose-ring in its nose. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abd al-Karim except Isra'il. And it has been narrated from Ibn Abbas, and from Salamah ibn al-Akwa', so we sufficed with the hadith of Ali."
"641","618 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gifted a silk cloak, so he sent it to me; then he saw it on me and said: I am not pleased for you what I dislike for myself; so he commanded me and I tore it among the women. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except Shu'bah."
"642","And from what al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated from Ibn Abi Layla from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. 619 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, he said: Fatimah complained of what she suffered from the mill's effect on her hand, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not find him, so she met A'ishah and informed her; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, A'ishah informed him of Fatimah's coming, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and we had taken our beds, so we went to stand, so he said: Stay in your place. So he sat between us until I felt the coolness of his foot on my chest, then he said: Shall I not teach you better than what you asked, when you take your beds, that you magnify thirty-four times, and glorify thirty-three times, and praise thirty-three times; it is better for you than a servant."
"643","620 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Abu Musa came to al-Hasan ibn Ali visiting him, so Ali said to him: Did you come visiting or gloating? If you came visiting, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man visits his Muslim brother, he is in the harvest of Paradise until he sits; when he sits, mercy covers him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels invoke blessings upon him until evening, and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels invoke blessings upon him until morning. And this hadith was narrated by Abu Mu'awiyah, from al-A'mash, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and Shu'bah narrated it from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Nafi', and this wording, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Ali, though it has been narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, through more than one channel."
"644","621 - Yusuf ibn Musa, and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever narrates from me a hadith while he thinks it is a lie, then he is one of the liars. And this hadith, thus narrated by Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, while others besides Ibn Abi Layla narrated it, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Samurah."
"645","622 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid, Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, when he sent me with the sacrificial camels, to slaughter them, and to give in charity their meat; so I sought his permission concerning their skins and their coverings, so he said: Give them in charity. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except Ash'ath ibn Sawwar."
"646","623 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. [Truncated in source: matn not present in this row; isnad only.]"
"647","624 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: I had two slave boys, brothers, so I wanted to sell one of them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell them both together or keep them both together. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, except Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah; and Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah did not hear anything from al-Hakam; and others besides al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated this hadith, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from a man, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. And Abu Khalid al-Dalani, and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated it, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"648","And from what Amr ibn Murrah narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali. 625 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed me, he said: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us until he placed his foot between me and Fatimah, then taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three tasbih, and thirty-three takbir, and thirty-three tahmid; so I have not left them since. Then a man said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? So he said: Not even the night of Siffin. And we do not know of Amr ibn Murrah narrating, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except this hadith."
"649","And from what Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Razi narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali. 626 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, judge of Rayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I heard the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I gathered, I and Fatimah, and al-Abbas, and Zayd ibn Harithah, then al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, my age has grown, and my bone has thinned, and my burden has increased; if you think, O Messenger of Allah, to order for me such-and-such sa' of food, then do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will do. Then Zayd ibn Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, you had given me land, my livelihood was from it, then you took it back; if you think to return it to me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We will do that. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you think to entrust me with this right which Allah made for you in His Book from this khums, so divide it in your standing, lest anyone dispute me after you, then do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We will do that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted it to me with its division in his lifetime, then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, entrusted it to me, so I divided it. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except from this channel with this isnad."
"650","And from what Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ali. 627 - Muhammad ibn Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you words, when you say them you will be forgiven, though you are already forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the High, the Mighty; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And this hadith has been narrated by others besides Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. End of the seventh part, and praise be to Allah as He deserves."
"651","And from what Abd al-A'la narrated from Muhammad ibn Ali, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali. 628 - Ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub, known as al-Samut, narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ali, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: The sun eclipsed, so Ali stood and bowed five bowings, and prostrated two prostrations, then did in the second rak'ah the like of that, then said: None prayed it after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but me. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla except Abd al-A'la, nor from Abd al-A'la except Isra'il."
"652","And from what Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated from Abd al-Rahman from Ali. 629 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad. 630 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy, so he said: In it is wudu, and wash it; and in maniy is ghusl."
"653","631 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ali, and Abu Mas'ud were sitting, then a funeral passed by them, so Abu Mas'ud stood, so Ali said to him: Sit. So he said: Did you not know that we used to stand for funerals? He said: That was only when you were Jews."
"654","632 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, and from Muslim ibn Salim, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali adjuring the people, saying: I adjure every Muslim man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm, except that he stood. So twelve men stood, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of Ali, then said: O people, am I not more worthy of the believers than themselves? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, whoever I am his master, then this is his master; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."
"655","And from what Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated, and he is Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. 633 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is purification, and its prohibition is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad."
"656","634 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from his father, from his grandfather Ali, he said: Much was said about Mariyah, mother of Ibrahim, concerning a Copt, a cousin of hers who used to visit her and come to her often, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Take this sword and go; if you find him with her, kill him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be in your command when you send me like a heated iron, nothing turning me back until I carry out what you commanded me, or does the witness see what the absent does not see? He said: Rather the witness sees what the absent does not see. So I came wearing the sword, and found him with her, so I drew the sword; when he saw me coming toward him, fearing that I wanted him, he went to a palm tree and climbed it, then threw himself on his back, then spread his legs, and he was castrated, smooth, having neither little nor much, so I sheathed the sword, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he said: Praise be to Allah who averts from us, the People of the House. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a connected channel from him except from this channel with this isnad."
"657","635 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Fajr prayer, then we would leave and none of us recognized another. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad."
"658","636 - Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"659","637 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running between al-Safa and al-Marwah. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad."
"660","638 - Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Madhari narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali: Have you seen this intercession that the people of Iraq speak of, is it true? He said: Which intercession? I said: The intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: True, by Allah, yes, by Allah, my uncle Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah narrated to me, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will intercede for my ummah until my Lord the Blessed and Exalted calls me, saying: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? So I will say: My Lord, I am pleased. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad from Ali."
"661","639 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and Muhammad ibn Ali Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of Ali, so he stood and bowed five bowings and prostrated two prostrations, then did in the second the like of that, then gave salam, then said: None prayed it after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but me. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad."
"662","640 - Musa ibn Abdullah Abu Talhah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhramah narrated to me, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father Muhammad ibn Ali, from his grandfather Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I never intended anything from what the people of Jahiliyyah used to do except twice; each time Allah came between me and what I wanted of that, then I never intended anything after that until Allah honoured me with His message. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated except from Ali with this isnad."
"663","641 - Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah, and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad ibn Ali, from their father, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mut'ah, and the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Abdullah, and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, except from this channel."
"664","642 - Muhammad ibn Umar al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"665","643 - Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah, and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad, from their father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade the mut'ah of women."
"666","644 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Yasin al-Zayyat al-Ijli narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The Mahdi is from us, the People of the House; Allah will set him right in a night. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this channel with this isnad, and we only wrote it despite the weakness of Yasin, for we did not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad, so for that we wrote it and clarified the defect in it."
"667","645 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Salim al-Makki, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, that he was asked about the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he said: He was neither short nor tall, of good hair, wavy, his face tinged with redness, large of joints, long of the line of hair on the chest, I never saw before him, nor saw after him the like of him; when he walked he leaned forward, as if descending a slope. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-Hajjaj, from Salim, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, except Abbad ibn al-Awwam."
"668","646 - al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in seven garments. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone corroborating Ibn Aqil on his narration, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Ibn Aqil with this isnad except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"669","647 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ya'la, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: My father sent me with a document to Uthman containing obligations, so he said: These are the obligations of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon which he used to send the collectors. So he said: We have no need of them. So I came to my father and informed him, so he said: Leave it. Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: Had Ali reviled him, he would have reviled him that day. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated with this wording except with this isnad."
"670","648 - al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Muhammad ibn Nashr, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a boy is born to you, give him my name and my kunyah as a gift. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Muhammad ibn Nashr except Layth, and we only know it from the hadith of Qays, from Layth."
"671","649 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Fitr, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, if a boy is born to me after you? He said: Give him my name and give him my kunyah. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Mundhir al-Thawri except Fitr ibn Khalifah."
"672","650 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, meaning al-Tha'labi, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so he said: Perform wudu from it and pray."
"673","651 - Amr ibn Abdullah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mundhir, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali. [Truncated in source: matn not present in this row; isnad only.]"
"674","652 - And Abu Kurayb narrated it to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he said: In it is wudu. And the hadith of Abd al-A'la, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Isra'il from him; and the hadith of Mundhir al-Thawri has been narrated by more than one, from Mundhir, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah."
"675","653 - Ali ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Salman, from Dinar Abu Umar, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw women at a funeral, so he said: Do you carry among those who carry? They said: No. He said: Then return, burdened with sin, without reward. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad, and more than one narrated it, from Isra'il, from Isma'il."
"676","654 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed me, from Isma'il ibn Salman, from Dinar Abu Umar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, in marfu' form, that he said: There is no people in whose house, or with them, there is a sheep, except that they are sanctified twice every day, or blessed upon twice, meaning: a milch sheep."
"677","655 - Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Salman narrated to us, from Dinar Abu Umar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, similar to it, and he did not raise it. And this Isma'il ibn Salman is a Kufi; Isra'il, and Qays, and Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah, and Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated from him, and he narrated three hadiths with isnad from Dinar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, while he narrates from Dinar, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, many hadiths."
"678","656 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given five that no Prophet before me was given: I was aided with awe, and I was given the comprehensive words, and spoils were made lawful for me, and he mentioned two qualities that escaped me, then he mentioned the hadith."
"679","657 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: When Hasan was born I named him Hamzah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you name my son? So I informed him. Then another was born to me, so he said: What did you name him? Or: did you name? So I mentioned to him, so he said: Name the first Hasan, and the other Husayn. And this hadith with this wording and this meaning, we do not know of it being narrated from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, except from this channel."
"680","658 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, he said: I asked Ali about mut'ah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced, or the announcer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced: that mut'ah is unlawful. And this hadith has been narrated by Abu Sa'd, and Ata al-Khurasani, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from his father, from Ali."
"681","659 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Ya'la, from Muhammad Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I commanded al-Miqdad, so he asked him, so he said: In it is wudu. And we do not know of al-Thawri narrating with isnad, from Hisham ibn Abi Ya'la, except this hadith."
"682","660 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Hibban, meaning Ibn Hilal, narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large of head, great of eyes, long of eyelashes, thick of beard, of luminous colour; when he walked he leaned forward, as if walking uphill; and when he turned he turned altogether; coarse of hands and feet, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, similar speech to it has been narrated from Ali with other than this isnad, and we do not know of it being narrated from Ibn Aqil, from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, except from this channel."
"683","661 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying toward a man, so he commanded him to repeat the prayer. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have prayed, while you were looking at me. And this speech, we do not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad, from Ali, so its meaning was: that the man was facing the praying person with his face, and did not move away from before his face, and pray."
"684","And from what Umar ibn Ali narrated from Ali. 662 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Awn narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father Muhammad ibn Umar, from his father, from Ali, he said: When it was the day of Badr, I fought something of fighting, then I came hastening to see what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had done, so I came and he was prostrating, saying: O Living, O Sustainer, O Living, O Sustainer, not adding to them. Then I returned to fighting, then I came while he was prostrating, saying that, then I went to fighting, then I returned, while he was saying that, so Allah gave him victory. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"685","663 - Harun ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ali ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, in marfu' form, so he said: The greatest visitation in reward is the lightest of it, and condolence is once. And I think Ibn Abi Fudayk did not hear from Ali ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib; and the speech, we do not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel."
"686","664 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from Umar ibn Ali: that he was with Ali ibn Abi Talib on a journey, so the sun set, so he marched until it darkened, then alighted and prayed Maghrib, then called for dinner and ate dinner, then prayed Isha, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he combined between the two prayers, or when he wanted to combine between the two prayers, did thus. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except with this isnad, and this speech is its wording and its meaning."
"687","665 - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: It was said to Ali: Describe for us the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: He was neither tall nor short, large of head, tinged with redness, long of eyelashes, thick of beard, of luminous colour; when he walked he leaned forward, and when he turned he turned altogether. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Umar except his son, and we only know it from the hadith of Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar, from his father, from his grandfather."
"688","666 - Abd Rabbihi ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour, no Muslim coinciding with it asking Allah therein except that He gives it to him."
"689","667 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs, from Umar ibn Ali, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded skulls to be set up in crops. He said: I said: For what reason? He said: Against the evil eye. And this hadith, we do not know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a connected channel except with this narration from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"690","And from what Ali ibn Alqamah narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib. 668 - Muhammad ibn Umar al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, when you confer privately with the Messenger, advance before your private conferring a charity}, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What do you think: a dinar, or what you find? I said: I cannot bear it. He said: Then how much? I said: A barley grain. He said: Indeed you are abstemious. He said: Then was revealed: {Are you afraid to advance before your private conferring charities} the verse. He said: So it was lightened through me for this ummah. And this hadith, we do not know it from the hadith of Ali except with this isnad connected, and Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, al-Thawri and Mis'ar and Sharik narrated from him, and a group, and we do not know of anyone narrating this speech from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali."
"691","669 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A mule was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What is this? They said: The donkey mounts the mare, so between them comes out this. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall not the donkey be put upon the mare? He said: Only those who do not understand do that. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from this channel with this isnad, nor from other than Ali."
"692","And from what Asim ibn Damrah narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. 670 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali. [Truncated in source: matn not present in this row; isnad only.]"
"693","671 - And al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated it to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah or al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed Allah is Odd and loves the odd. And we do not know of Mansur narrating from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, except this hadith; and it is narrated from Abu Sa'id, and from Abu Hurayrah, and from others."
"694","And from what al-A'mash narrated from Abu Ishaq. 672 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: We said to Ali: How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: You cannot bear it. We said: Inform us. He said: You cannot bear it. So we repeated that to him several times, so he said: When the sun was from here, its measure from here, meaning: the west, he prayed two rak'ahs, then he waited until when it was here, by its measure at Zuhr, he prayed four, then he stayed until when the shadow came and the sun declined, he prayed four, then he prayed before Asr four. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra, though more than one has narrated it from Abu Ishaq."
"695","673 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim ibn Damrah, he said: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by day, so he said: You will not be able to bear that. He said: We said: Whoever of us is able to do that. He said: So he said: When the sun was from here, like its state from here at Asr, he prayed two rak'ahs; and when the sun was from here, like its state from here at Zuhr, he prayed four; and he prayed before Zuhr four, and after it two, and before Asr four, separating between every two rak'ahs with salam upon the close angels, and those who followed them of the Prophets and the Messengers. And we do not know of this speech and this act being narrated except from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"696","674 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he used to pray after every obligatory prayer two rak'ahs, except Asr and Fajr. And we do not know of anyone narrating this speech from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali, from the hadith of Asim ibn Ali."
"697","675 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: Ali was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the voluntary by day, so he said: And who can bear that? He said: We can bear of it what we are able. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun was from here, by its measure of the Asr prayer, prayed two rak'ahs, giving salam in them upon the close angels, and the Prophets and the Messengers, and those who followed them of the believers and the Muslims; and when forenoon rose, and the sun was from here, like its state, from here at Zuhr, he prayed four, separating between them with salam upon the close angels, the believers and the Messengers, and those who followed them of the believers and the Messengers; and when the sun declined he prayed four before Zuhr, and prayed after Zuhr two rak'ahs, doing in them the like of that; and before Asr four, doing in them the like of that, separating between every two rak'ahs with salam upon the close angels, and the Prophets and the Messengers, and those who followed them of the believers and the Muslims. And this hadith was narrated by al-A'mash, and Shu'bah, and al-Thawri, and Isra'il."
"698","676 - As for the hadith of Isra'il, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim ibn Damrah narrating from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"699","677 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, he said: I asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by day, so he said: You will never be able to bear that. I said: Whoever of us is able to do that. He said: When the sun was from here, like its state, from here, he prayed two rak'ahs; and when the sun was from here, like its state, from here at Zuhr, he prayed Zuhr, he prayed four; praying before Zuhr four, and after it two, and before Asr four, separating between every two rak'ahs with taslim upon the close angels, and the Prophets and the Messengers, and those who followed them of the believers and the Muslims; so that is twelve rak'ahs. And we do not know of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrating with isnad, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Abd al-Malik except Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"700","678 - Fahm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing in one hundred and ninety of silver; when it reaches two hundred, therein is five dirhams."
"701","679 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is nothing in one hundred and ninety of silver; when it reaches two hundred, therein is five dirhams. And we do not know of anyone narrating this wording which Asim ibn Damrah narrated, from Ali, other than Asim, from Ali; nor did anyone narrate this wording, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali."
"702","680 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr at every part of the night; from its beginning, and its middle, and its end, then his witr ended at its end."
"703","681 - Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr at the beginning of the night, and its middle, and its end, then witr became established for him at its end. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali except from the hadith of Asim ibn Damrah from him."
"704","682 - Yusuf ibn Musa, and Abu Kurayb narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that he was asked about witr, is it obligatory? He said: As for obligation, no; but it is a sunnah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practised, and his companions, until they passed upon that."
"705","683 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: Witr is not imperative, but it is a sunnah."
"706","684 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, that he said: Witr is not an obligation, but it is a sunnah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practised."
"707","685 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Tha'labah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: Witr is not imperative, but it is a sunnah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practised, and the Muslims after him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, and more than one narrated it, from Abu Ishaq."
"708","686 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali. [Truncated in source: matn not present in this row; isnad only.]"
"709","687 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to flog a slave-girl of his who committed zina, so I flogged her after she recovered from her childbirth. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"710","688 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the month of patience, and three days of every month, removes the rancour of the chest. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, nor from al-Hajjaj except Hammad ibn Salamah; and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated it, from his father, from al-Harith, from Ali."
"711","689 - Yusuf ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray any prayer except that he prayed after it two rak'ahs, except Fajr and Asr."
"712","690 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In what the sky waters, or a conquest, meaning: or it was a conquest, therein is the tenth; and what is watered by the camel-drawn well, therein is half the tenth. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, as mawquf; and Muhammad ibn Salim raised it with isnad; and Zuhayr said, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, he said: And I think he raised it."
"713","691 - Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim narrated it to us, he said: Shuja' ibn al-Walid Abu Badr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: And I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"714","692 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four before Zuhr. And we do not know of Mis'ar narrating with isnad from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, except this hadith."
"715","693 - Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves postponement for him in his term, and increase in his provision, let him join his kinship. And this hadith is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels, and the highest narrated in that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is what Ali narrated from him, upon him be peace. And it has been narrated from Ali through another way, and I do not think Ibn Jurayj heard this hadith from Habib, and we do not know of anyone narrating it other than him."
"716","694 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, and Bishr ibn Adam, and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Do not expose your thigh, nor look at the thigh of the living, nor the dead. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"717","695 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Sinan, meaning: his father, narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah sent Yahya ibn Zakariyya to the Children of Isra'il with five words; when He sent Isa, Allah the Blessed and Exalted said: O Isa, say to Yahya ibn Zakariyya: Either you convey what you were sent with to the Children of Isra'il, or I convey to them. So Yahya went out until he reached the Children of Isra'il, and said: Indeed Allah commands you to worship Him, and not to associate anything with Him; and the parable of that is like a man who freed a man, and did good to him and gave him, then he went and disbelieved his benefactor, and befriended another; and indeed Allah commands you to establish prayer, and the parable of that is like a man whom the enemy captured, and wanted to kill him, so he said: Do not kill me, for I have a treasure, and I ransom myself, so he gave them his treasure, and saved himself; and indeed Allah the Blessed and Exalted commands you to give charity, and the parable of that is like a man who walked to his enemy, having taken a shield for fighting, so he does not care from where he is approached; and indeed Allah commands you to recite the Book, and the parable of that is like a people in their fortress, their enemy coming to them, having prepared in every corner of the fortress people, so their enemy does not come to them from any corner except that before them are those who repel them from the fortress; so that is the parable of one who recites the Quran, ever in the most fortified fortress, or in a fortified fortress. Abu Bakr said: And I did not see the fifth in my book. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad. [Flag: source text itself notes the fifth word missing from transmitter's book.]"
"718","And what al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd narrated from Ali. 696 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad; and al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, we do not know of anyone narrating with isnad from him, except this Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, and he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq Abu Shaybah, and he is a Wasiti, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, and Muhammad ibn Fudayl, and Abu Mu'awiyah, and al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani, and Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated from him, a righteous in hadith."
"719","697 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been forbidden to recite in bowing and prostration; so when you bow, magnify Allah, and when you prostrate, strive in supplication, for it is worthy that it be answered for you. And we do not know of this speech being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"720","698 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you is he who learns the Quran and teaches it. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad."
"721","699 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard a man saying to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: O Commander of the Faithful, which month do you command me to fast after the month of Ramadan? So Ali said: I never heard anyone asking about this after a man I heard asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which month do you command me to fast after the month of Ramadan? So he said: If you are fasting after Ramadan, then fast the month of Muharram; for it is the month of Allah, and in it Allah turned to a people. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Ali with this isnad."
"722","700 - Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you is every much-tested, oft-repenting. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali; and some of those who transmitted from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq raised it, and some of them stopped it, and Abd al-Wahid stopped it."
"723","701 - Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, do not follow the glance with the glance; for you only have the first glance. And this hadith, we heard it only from Abbad, from Muhammad ibn Fadl."
"724","702 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, and Sadaqah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there are chambers, their outside seen from their inside, and their inside from their outside. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, those are the dwellings of the Prophets. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah prepared them for whoever feeds food, and spreads salam, and persists in fasting, and prays at night while people sleep. And this hadith, we do not know of it being narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this isnad; Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, is alone with it."
"725","703 - Abu Kurayb, and al-Hasan ibn Arafah, and Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi, and Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Paradise there is a market, wherein there is neither buying nor selling except images; whoever loves an image enters into it, or desires an image enters into it; and for the houris is a gathering in which they gather, raising voices the like of which none heard, saying: We are the everlasting, so we do not die; and we are the blissful, so we do not despair; and we are the pleased, so we do not anger; so glad tidings for whoever was for us, and we were for him. And this hadith, we do not know of anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali with this isnad. And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated it, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from Ali, as mawquf."
"726","704 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated it to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from 'Ali, as a stopped (mawquf) report."
"727","And among what 'Abdullah ibn Salamah narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: 705 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Salih ibn Huyayy, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O 'Ali, shall I not teach you words which, when you say them, you will be forgiven, although you are already forgiven? There is no god but You, the Most High, the Most Great; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Great Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And we do not know of Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrating from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, except two hadiths, this being one of them; and Nusayar ibn Abi al-Ash'ath narrated it from Abu Ishaq."
"728","706 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi, Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj, narrated to us, he said: Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, and 'Uqbah ibn Khalid both narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Qur'an; Hafs said: in every state except janabah, and 'Uqbah said: except when he was junub."
"729","707 - And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Hafs and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"730","708 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself, then recite the Qur'an, and eat with us, and nothing would prevent him from reciting the Qur'an except janabah; the meaning of 'laysa' is 'except janabah.' And we do not know of this hadith with this wording being narrated except from 'Ali, nor being narrated from 'Ali except through the hadith of 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali; and 'Amr ibn Murrah used to narrate from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, saying: his hadith is partly recognized and partly rejected."
"731","709 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, he said: I was ill, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me while I was saying: O Allah, if my appointed time has come then have mercy on me, and if it is delayed then make me content, and if it is a trial then grant me patience. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you say? I repeated it to him, and he struck me with his foot and said: Say: O Allah, grant me well-being - or he said: Heal him - and I never complained of that pain of mine afterward."
"732","710 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Faryabi Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know of anyone narrating these words except 'Ali with this chain, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah except 'Amr ibn Murrah."
"733","711 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi al-Miqdam, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me while I am young and they are elders, and I have no knowledge of speech (judicial address)? He said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will guide your heart and make your tongue firm. He said: By Allah, I never became at a loss for words about anything afterward. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, except Abu Ishaq, nor from Abu Ishaq except 'Amr ibn Abi al-Miqdam; and it has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels."
"734","712 - Abu Tahir 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Ya'la ibn 'Ata al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O assembly of women, fear Allah and seek the pleasure of your husbands, for if a woman knew what her husband's right is, she would remain standing as long as his lunch and dinner are present. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"735","And what Qays ibn 'Ubad narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: 713 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah. 714 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Qays ibn 'Ubad, he said: I set out, I and al-Ashtar, to 'Ali, and we said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust to you anything he did not entrust to the people in general? He said: No, except what is in this book of mine; so he brought out a book from the scabbard of his sword, and in it was: The Muslims, their blood is equal, and the lowest of them grants protection binding upon them; no believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant; whoever commits an offense, it is upon himself, and whoever shelters an offender, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. And it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah, and from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, and from others, so we mentioned it from 'Ali and sufficed with it; and this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels, and this chain is the best and most authentic chain narrated in that regard; and we do not know of Qays ibn 'Ubad narrating from 'Ali except two hadiths, this being one of them and the other being the next."
"736","715 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated it to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn 'Ubad, from 'Ali, he said: It was revealed concerning me, and Hamzah, and 'Ubaydah ibn al-Harith, and 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, and al-Walid ibn 'Utbah: These are two disputants who disputed concerning their Lord. And al-Mu'tamir narrated this hadith from his father, from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn 'Ubad, without saying: from 'Ali; and Abu Hashim al-Rummani narrated it from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn 'Ubad, from Abu Dharr."
"737","And among what Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi narrated from 'Ali: 716 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Harami ibn 'Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn 'Umayrah narrated to us, he said: Maymun al-Kurdi narrated to me, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from 'Ali, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was holding my hand, and we passed by a garden, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful this garden is! He said: For you in Paradise is one more beautiful than it. Then we passed by another, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful this garden is! He said: For you in Paradise is one more beautiful than it, until we passed by seven gardens, each time I saying how beautiful it was, and he saying: For you in Paradise is one more beautiful than it. Then when the road was clear for him, he embraced me, then burst out weeping; I said: O Messenger of Allah, what makes you weep? He said: Rancor in the hearts of people, which they will not show to you except after me. I said: While my religion is safe? He said: While your religion is safe. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; nor do we know of Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi narrating from 'Ali except this."
"738","And among what Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali narrated from 'Ali: 717 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from his father, from 'Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the nursing infant: the urine of the boy is sprinkled over, and the urine of the girl is washed. And this action has been narrated by 'A'ishah and Abu Layla, and Zaynab bint Jahsh, and Anas ibn Malik, and Umm Qays bint Mihsan, and Umm al-Fadl, and their chains are close; and the best of them in chain is the hadith of 'Ali and the hadith of Umm Qays. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain; and only Mu'adh ibn Hisham raised it as a chain from his father, while others narrated it from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb, from his father, from 'Ali, as a stopped report."
"739","718 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: A Kufan of ours called 'Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib saying: 'Abdullah ibn Salam said to me, while I had placed my foot in the stirrup: Do not go to Iraq, for if you go to it, the fly of the sword will strike you there. He said: By Allah, he indeed said it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said it to me before him. Abu al-Aswad said: I said: By Allah, I have never seen a fighting man narrating this except you. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith except 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, with this chain; nor do we know of anyone narrating it except 'Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan from Abu Harb, nor anyone narrating it from 'Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan except Ibn 'Uyaynah."
"740","And among what Harithah ibn Mudarrib narrated from 'Ali: 719 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: When we arrived in Madinah, we found it unhealthy and were struck by fever there; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek news about Quraysh, and it reached him that they had camped at Badr, which is a well. So he sent two men, one of them al-Zubayr, and the other Abu Ishaq thinks was 'Ali, and they captured two men: a man of Quraysh and a freed slave of 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt. The Qurashi slipped away, and they brought the freed slave, and they began asking him, saying to him: How many are the people, or how many are they? He would say: By Allah, they are many in number, severe in might, until they brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who asked him, and he said that. He said: How many camels do the people slaughter each day? He said: Ten camels. He said: A camel for a hundred; the people are a thousand. He said: A light rain fell upon us in the night, and we scattered beneath the low trees; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent his night supplicating, saying: O Allah, if You destroy this band, You will not be worshipped on earth. Then when dawn broke, he said: Prayer, O servants of Allah. So we came forward from beneath the trees and low growth, and he urged and encouraged fighting, and said: It is as if I am looking at their fallen ones. He said: When the people drew near, there was among them a man riding through the people on a red camel; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Zubayr: Call one of your companions and ask him: Who is the owner of the red camel? If there is among the people anyone who commands you to good, it is he. Al-Zubayr asks: Who is the owner of the red camel? They said: 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and he is forbidding fighting, saying: O people, I see a people ready to die; by Allah, I do not think you will reach them before you perish. He said: When what he said reached Abu Jahl, he came to him and said: Your lungs are filled with fear now that you have seen Muhammad and his companions. 'Utbah said to him: Is it me you taunt, O you with the dyed backside? You will know which of us is more cowardly. So 'Utbah dismounted from his camel, followed by his brother Shaybah and his son al-Walid, and they called for single combat. Some youths of the Ansar rushed to them; he said: Who are you? They told him, and he said: We have no need of you; we want only our cousins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand, O Hamzah; stand, O 'Ali; stand, O 'Ubaydah ibn al-Harith. He said: Hamzah advanced to 'Utbah, I advanced to Shaybah, and 'Ubaydah advanced to al-Walid. He said: Hamzah did not linger with his opponent before finishing him; and I did not linger with my opponent; and al-Walid and 'Ubaydah exchanged two blows, each wounding his opponent. He said: I and Hamzah advanced to them both, finished off al-Walid, and carried 'Ubaydah away. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"741","720 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib you are able to take captive, for they were only brought out under compulsion. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from 'Ali except Harithah ibn Mudarrib, nor do we know of anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Ali."
"742","721 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: You send me to a people older than me, so how shall I judge among them? He said: Go, for Allah will guide your heart and make your tongue firm. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from Harithah ibn Mudarrib except Abu Ishaq, nor from Abu Ishaq except Isra'il; and it has been narrated from 'Ali by more than one, and the best chain narrated from 'Ali is this chain."
"743","722 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give to a people to reconcile their hearts, and I leave a people to what is with them - or: to what Allah has placed in their hearts - among them Furat ibn Hayyan. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith with this chain from 'Ali except Dirar ibn Surad, from Yahya ibn al-Yaman."
"744","723 - And Isra'il narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali, he said: When the fighting grew fierce, and the two sides met, we would shield ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would not see anyone closer to the enemy than him. My father narrated it to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from 'Ali."
"745","And among what Hubayrah ibn Yarim narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 724 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wake his family in the last ten nights of Ramadan."
"746","725 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from 'Ali, with the like of it. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except with this chain; and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning his i'tikaf through other channels: from 'A'ishah through several channels, and from Abu Sa'id, Abu Hurayrah, Abu Layla, and Anas."
"747","726 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from 'Ali: that a garment of silk was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent it to me, and I wore it; he saw it on me and said: I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself; so he commanded me, and I tore it up among the women. And this hadith has been narrated through other channels from 'Ali with different wordings."
"748","727 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: Hubayrah and the companions of 'Ali narrated to me, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the ji'ah; and the ji'ah is to make nabidh from wheat and barley until it intoxicates. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this wording and this chain."
"749","728 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating that he heard Hubayrah narrating from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the mitharah, and qassi garments, and gold rings."
"750","And among what Abu Salih al-Hanafi narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 729 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu 'Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me and to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, on the day of Badr: With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il, and Israfil is a great angel witnessing the fighting, or being in the ranks. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain; and more than one narrated it to us from Abu Ahmad."
"751","730 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed me, from Abu 'Awn al-Thaqafi, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, he said: 'Ali said to the people: Ask me. So Ibn al-Kawwa' said: Tell us about the two owned sisters, and about the brother's daughter through breastfeeding. He said: You are going astray in the wilderness. He said: We only ask you about what we do not know; as for what we know, we do not ask you about it. He said: As for the two owned sisters, a verse forbade them both, and a verse permitted them both, so I neither permit it, nor forbid it, nor command it, nor forbid it, nor do it myself, nor anyone of my household; and as for the brother's daughter through breastfeeding, I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is my brother's daughter through breastfeeding. And this hadith, concerning the story of Hamzah's daughter, has been narrated from 'Ali through several channels."
"752","731 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from 'Ali, he said: A sira' garment was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gifted it to me, and I wore it; I saw dislike on his face, then once he said: so I made it into head coverings among my women, and once he said: I split it among my women."
"753","And among what Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 732 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, that they dug a well in Yemen, and a lion fell into it, and they awoke looking at it; then a man fell into the well and clung to a man, and the other clung to another, until they were four, and they all fell into the well together, and the lion wounded them; then a man took it with his spear and killed it. The people said to the first: You killed our companions, and their blood money is upon you, but his companions refused, and they almost fought. 'Ali arrived in that situation, and they asked him, so he said: I will judge among you with a judgment; whoever of you is pleased with it, his pleasure binds him, and whoever is displeased has no right until they come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to judge among you. They said: Yes. He said: Collect, from those present at the well among the people, a quarter of a blood money, a third of a blood money, half a blood money, and a full blood money: for the first a quarter of a blood money, because three perished above him; for the second a third of a blood money, because two perished above him; for the third half a blood money, because one perished above him; and for the last the full blood money. If you are pleased, this is a judgment among you; and if you are not pleased, you have no right until you come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to judge among you. So they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the next year and told him; he said: I will judge among you, Allah willing - while he was sitting at the station of Ibrahim - and a man stood and said: 'Ali judged among us. He said: How did 'Ali judge among you? They told him, and he said: It is as he judged among you. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor do we know of a path from 'Ali except through this channel."
"754","733 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Hanash, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: You send me to a people I am not the eldest of, and I have no knowledge of judgment? He said: When two disputants come to you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says. He said: I have remained a judge ever since, and never doubted in a judgment between two. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Simak, from Hanash, from 'Ali; among them Sharik, Za'idah, and Sulayman ibn Mu'adh; and Asbat narrated from Simak, from Hanash, from 'Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with him the declaration of disavowal to the people of Makkah."
"755","And among what Abu Hayyah ibn Qays narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 734 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, that 'Ali performed ablution three times three times, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution."
"756","735 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah, that 'Ali performed ablution three times three times, and wiped over his head, and said: Whoever is pleased to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is like this."
"757","736 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, that he saw 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in al-Rahbah perform ablution: he washed his hands, then rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, his forearms three times three times, his head three times, and washed his feet to the ankles three times three times; then he stood and drank the remainder of his ablution water while standing, and said: I wanted to show you how the purification of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. Abu Ishaq said: 'Abd Khayr narrated to me from 'Ali with the like of this hadith, except that when he finished, he took a bowlful of water in his palm and drank it while standing. And we do not know of anyone narrating these words from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from 'Ali, except Abu al-Ahwas."
"758","737 - And Isra'il narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, he said: I saw 'Ali come to al-Rahbah and urinate standing, then perform ablution: rinsed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, drank standing, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do. And al-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Habbah ibn Qays, from 'Ali, another hadith."
"759","738 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, he said: Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hayyah ibn Qays, from 'Ali, he said: I used to draw a bucket of water for a date, stipulating that it be sweet and firm."
"760","And among what Hani ibn Hani narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him: 739 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from 'Ali, he said: 'Ammar asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The pure, the made pure."
"761","740 - Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Aththam ibn 'Ali informed me, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from 'Ali, that 'Ammar ibn Yasir asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Permit the pure, the made pure, filled with faith to his marrow. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali; and Hani ibn Hani, we do not know of anyone narrating from him except Abu Ishaq."
"762","741 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym and Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from 'Ali, he said: 'Ammar asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Permit the pure, the made pure. Abu Nu'aym said in his hadith: Welcome to the pure, the made pure. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from 'Ali except Hani ibn Hani, and more than one narrated it from Abu Ishaq. As for the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Ishaq, we do not know of anyone narrating it from al-A'mash except 'Aththam ibn 'Ali, and he added in it: filled with faith to his marrow; nor do we know of anyone narrating from Hani ibn Hani except Abu Ishaq."
"763","742 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from 'Ali, he said: When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb; he said: Rather he is Hasan. Then when al-Husayn was born, I named him Harb, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? We said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Husayn. Then when the third was born, I named him Harb, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Show me my son; what did you name him? We said: Harb. He said: Rather he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them with the names of Harun's sons: Jabbar, Jubayr, and Mujabbir. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a better chain than this chain with this wording, although Hani ibn Hani, we have already mentioned that none narrated from him except Abu Ishaq; and it has been narrated from 'Ali through another channel, and narrated from Salman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and the hadith of Hani is the best narrated in that regard."
"764","743 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' ibn Hani, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb, and I liked to take the kunyah Abu Harb; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and did tahnik for him, and said: What did you name my son? We said: Harb. He said: He is al-Hasan. Then al-Husayn was born, and I named him Harb; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and did tahnik for him, and said: What did you name my son? We said: Harb. He said: He is al-Husayn. And this hadith, Qays added in it: and I liked to take the kunyah Abu Harb; and in it is that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did tahnik for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"765","744 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, I and Ja'far and Zayd, and said to Zayd: Our brother and our freedman; so Zayd hopped. And he said to Ja'far: You resemble my creation and my character; so he hopped behind Zayd's hopping. Then he said to me: You are from me and I am from you; so I hopped behind Ja'far's hopping. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, with this chain."
"766","And among what Habbah al-'Urani narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 745 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah. 746 - And Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated it to us, he said: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Habbah al-'Urani, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except with this chain."
"767","747 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Muslim, from Habbah al-'Urani, from 'Ali. [The matn is not stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"768","748 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Muslim, from Habbah, meaning Ibn Juwayn, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to eat garlic; he said: Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from 'Ali with this chain."
"769","749 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' and 'Amr ibn Abi al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Abi al-Miqdam, from Habbah, meaning Ibn Juwayn, he said: I heard 'Ali saying: I leaned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against my chest, and he said to me: O 'Ali, I enjoin upon you good toward the Arabs. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except with this chain; and this Abu al-Miqdam, his name is Thabit, and he is Thabit al-Haddad; Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from him, and he is the father of 'Amr ibn Thabit."
"770","750 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abi al-Miqdam, from Habbah, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and command them to close their doors. So I went and told them, and they did, except Hamzah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, they did, except Hamzah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell Hamzah to move his door. So I told him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to move your door, and he moved it. I returned to him while he was standing praying, and he said: Return to your house. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording except from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him; nor do we know of anyone narrating it from 'Ali except Habbah; and Habbah, Salamah ibn Kuhayl and Muslim al-Mula'i and Abu al-Miqdam narrated from him."
"771","751 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Habbah al-'Urani saying: I saw 'Ali ibn Abi Talib addressing, and he laughed a laugh, and we were amazed at his laughing; when he came down, we said: O Commander of the Believers, you laughed a laugh upon the pulpit, so what did you laugh at? He said: I remembered Abu Talib; I saw myself with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the prayer came, the 'Asr prayer, and we had come to a place called Nakhlah - I think he said: we wanted to pray - and Abu Talib said to us, looking at us: O sons of my brother, what are you doing? We said: We pray. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him to Islam, and he said: What you call me to is good, but by Allah, O son of my brother, my backside will never be above (me). So I laughed at his words. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali; nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Habbah except Salamah ibn Kuhayl."
"772","752 - And Shu'bah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Habbah, from 'Ali, he said: The first prayer we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was 'Asr; Shu'bah narrated it shortened. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah, from Habbah, from 'Ali."
"773","And among what Hujayyah ibn 'Adi narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 753 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shu'bah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn 'Adi, he said: A man asked 'Ali about the cow, and he said: For seven. He said: The one with broken horn. He said: It does not harm you. He said: The lame. He said: When it reaches the rite; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear."
"774","754 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Bishr ibn Adam and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn 'Adi, he said: I asked 'Ali, or a man asked 'Ali, about the cow, and he said: For seven. He said: The horn. He said: It does not harm you. He said: Lameness. He said: When it reaches the rite; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah, from 'Ali; nor do we know of Abu Ishaq narrating a supported hadith from Salamah except this hadith, nor anyone narrating it from Abu Ishaq except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"775","755 - Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when morning came he would say: O Allah, by You we enter morning, and by You we enter evening, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the resurrection. And he would say in the evening the like of that, and say at its end: And to You is the return. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel; nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Salamah except Ibn Abi Layla."
"776","And among what Abu Khalifah narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 756 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Umar ibn Kaysan al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Abu Khalifah, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness. And we do not know of Abu Khalifah narrating from 'Ali except this hadith, nor any chain for him except this chain."
"777","The remainder of the Musnad of 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. And among what al-Sa'ib ibn Malik narrated from 'Ali: 757 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to Fatimah and said to her: I complain of my chest from drawing water with the bucket. She said: And I, by Allah, complain of my hands from grinding with the mill. So 'Ali said to her: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him to give you a servant. So she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), greeted him, then returned; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What brought you? She said: I came to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When she returned to 'Ali, she said: By Allah, I could not speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) out of awe of him. So they both went to him together, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What brought you both; there must have come - I think he said - a need with you both. So 'Ali said to him: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; I complained to Fatimah of my hands from drawing with the bucket, and she complained to me of her hands from grinding with the mill, so we came to you to give us a servant from what Allah has given you. He said: No, but I spend - or: I spend it - upon the people of al-Suffah whose stomachs are folded from hunger, and I find nothing to feed them. He said: When they returned and took their beds at night, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them while they were in a khamil - and the khamil is a velvet cloth - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had furnished her with it and with a pillow stuffed with idhkhir; and 'Ali and Fatimah had been grieved when he turned them away. When they heard the sound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they went to rise, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Stay in your place. Then he came until he sat at the edge of the khamil, then said: You came to me for me to give you a servant, and I will guide you - or a word like it - to what is better for you than a servant: you praise Allah after every prayer ten times, and glorify ten times, and magnify ten times; or you glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times, making one hundred, when you take your bed at night. So 'Ali said: I do not know that I left it afterward. 'Abdullah ibn al-Kawwa' said to him: Not even on the night of Siffin? 'Ali said to him: May Allah fight you; not even on the night of Siffin. And this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels with different wordings; nor do we know of it being narrated with this wording except from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from 'Ali."
"778","And among what Rabi'ah ibn Najid narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 758 - al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Zayyat narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Mula'i narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: O 'Ali, in you is a likeness from 'Isa son of Maryam: the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him in a station that is not his. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except with this chain."
"779","759 - Ibrahim ibn Hani' narrated to us, he said: al-Fayd ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabi'ah ibn Najid, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh: the righteous of them are rulers of their righteous, and the wicked of them are rulers of their wicked. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"780","760 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, he said: 'Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Aws ibn Aws - thus he said - from 'Ali: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The blood of 'Ammar and his flesh are forbidden for the Fire to consume. And we do not know of these words being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know of Abu Ishaq narrating from Aws ibn Aws anything; this only came as an error from 'Ata ibn Muslim, who was not problematic but was not a preserver."
"781","And among what Muhammad ibn 'Aqil narrated from 'Ali: 761 - 'Abdullah ibn Abi Thumamah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Abdullah al-Muqri' al-'Ijli narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, he said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: O people, tell me of the bravest of people? They said - or he said: we said - You, O Commander of the Believers. He said: Indeed, I never faced anyone in single combat except I took my due from him, but tell me of the bravest of people. They said: We do not know; so who? He said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him; on the day of Badr, we made a shelter for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said: Who will be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night, lest one of the polytheists pounce upon him? By Allah, none approached him except Abu Bakr, brandishing a sword over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); none pounced toward him except he pounced toward him. So this is the bravest of people. Then 'Ali said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Quraysh seized him - this one pushing him and this one shaking him - saying: Are you the one who made the gods one god? He said: By Allah, none approached him except Abu Bakr, striking this one and pushing this one and shaking this one, saying: Woe to you, do you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah? Then 'Ali raised a cloak that was upon him and wept until his beard became wet, then said: I adjure you by Allah, is the believer of the household of Pharaoh better, or Abu Bakr? The people fell silent, and he said: Will you not answer me? By Allah, an hour of Abu Bakr is better than the earth full of the like of the believer of the household of Pharaoh: that one was a man who concealed his faith, and this one is a man who proclaimed his faith. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"782","And among what Abu Jamilah, whose name is Maysarah, narrated from 'Ali: 762 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah, he said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A slave girl of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed an offense, meaning she fornicated, so he commanded me to carry out the hadd upon her; I came to her while her blood had not yet dried, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: When she dries, carry out the hadd upon her. And he said: Carry out the hadd punishments upon those your right hands possess. And this hadith has been narrated by al-Thawri, and Abu al-Ahwas, and Abu Waki', from 'Abd al-A'la, from Abu Jamilah, from 'Ali."
"783","763 - Zayd ibn Akhzam and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa' narrated to us, from 'Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Jamilah, from 'Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and he commanded me, so I gave the cupper his wage. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"784","And among what 'Abbad ibn 'Abdullah al-Asadi narrated from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: 764 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abbad ibn 'Abdullah al-Asadi, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that with him on Friday was Zayd ibn Suhan, while he was addressing upon a pulpit of brick, with the freed slaves around him. He said: A man spoke some words - and I do not know what the words were - and he became angry until his face reddened. He said: He fell silent; and while we were thus, al-Ash'ath ibn Qays came stepping over the people and said: These red ones have overcome your face. Zayd ibn Suhan struck my shoulders and said: To Allah we belong; by Allah, the Arabs will surely reveal what they used to conceal. Then he said: Who will excuse me from these fat ones? One of them turns over on his bed, while a people go early to the remembrance of Allah; what do you command me - shall I drive them away and be among the wrongdoers? Then he said: By the One who split the seed and created the soul, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: They will surely strike you away from the religion in return, as you struck them for it at the beginning. And this hadith with these words, we do not know of anyone narrating it except al-Minhal, from 'Abbad, from 'Ali."
"785","765 - He said: And I heard Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrating from one of his companions, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abbad ibn 'Abdullah al-Asadi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me the dubba', the muzaffat, and the hantam."
"786","766 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from 'Abbad ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Ali, concerning the word of Allah, blessed and exalted is He: And warn your nearest kin: he called them and gathered them over a lamb's thigh and a cup of milk, although among them was one who would eat a young camel. He said: We ate until we were full, and drank until satisfied. Thus Sharik narrated it from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from 'Abbad, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"787","And among what Abu Maryam al-Hanafi narrated from 'Ali: 767 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Samut narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq al-Basri al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Maryam al-Hanafi, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The wife of al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of her husband that he beats her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go to him and say: The Prophet, peace be upon him, says such-and-such. She went, then returned and said: He has returned to beating me. He said: Go and say to him: The Prophet, peace be upon him, says such-and-such. She went, then returned and said: He has returned to beating me."
"788","768 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the wife of al-Walid ibn 'Uqbah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of al-Walid. He said to her: Return and say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has granted me protection. She went and stayed a while, then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has not desisted from me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut a fringe from his garment and said: Go with this and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a fringe from my garment. She went and stayed a while, then returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has only increased me in beating. So he raised his hands and said: O Allah, deal with al-Walid - twice or thrice. And these words, we do not know of anyone narrating them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him; nor is it narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain. And in this hadith, of jurisprudence, is the permissibility of a claim against an opponent when he is not present with his adversary, because the fringe from his garment is summoning him to attend, like a ring."
"789","769 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from 'Ali, he said: I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night until we came to the Ka'bah. He said to me: Sit. Then I lifted him up; when he saw my weakness beneath him, he said: Sit. So I sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down from me and sat for me and said: Climb upon my shoulders. So I climbed upon him; then he rose with me until it seemed to me that if I wished, I could reach the horizon of the sky. I climbed the House and came to the idol of Quraysh, a statue of a man of brass or copper, and I kept working at it, right and left, from before it and behind it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come on. While I worked at it, he said: Throw it down. So I threw it down, and it broke as glass breaks. Then we went hastening until we hid among the houses; and nothing of those idols was placed upon it afterward. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording except from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this chain."
"790","770 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Hakim, from Abu Maryam, from 'Ali, he said: We came to Khaybar; when he, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to it, he sent 'Umar with the people, and they did not tarry before 'Umar and his companions were defeated. He said: I will surely send to them a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; he will fight them until Allah grants him victory. He said: The people craned their necks for it and stretched their necks. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed a while, then said: Where is 'Ali? They said: He has ophthalmia. He said: Call him to me. When I came to him, he opened my eyes, then spat in them, then gave me the banner. I went until I came to them, and among them was Marhab chanting, until we met; Allah killed him, his companions fled and fortified themselves, closing the gate. We came to the gate, and I kept working at it until Allah opened it. And this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, through other channels with other than this wording."
"791","And among what 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Asadi narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 771 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah informed me, he said: 'Ali mounted me behind him, then traveled in the desert of Kufah, then raised his head to the sky and said: O Allah, forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Then he turned to me and laughed. I said: What is this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted me behind him, then raised his head and said: Forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Then he turned to me and laughed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, your seeking forgiveness from your Lord and your turning to me laughing? He said: I laughed at the laughing of my Lord, blessed and exalted is He, at His servant, for He knew that none forgives sins but He."
"792","772 - And 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Taymi al-Madani narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam, meaning al-'Urani, narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from 'Ali, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, with traces of khaluq upon him, and he refused to pledge him. He went and washed the traces of khaluq from himself, then came and he pledged him. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"793","773 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah al-Asadi, he said: I saw 'Ali brought a mount; he placed his foot upon it, and when he was settled, he said: Praise be to Allah: Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it; and to our Lord we shall return. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he mounted his mount, do like this. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali; and the best chain narrated from 'Ali is this chain."
"794","774 - 'Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me fighting the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the hadith of 'Ali ibn Rabi'ah, from 'Ali, except with this chain; and we heard it only from 'Abbad ibn Ya'qub."
"795","And among what Abu Fakhitah narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 775 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except with this chain."
"796","776 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved to recite: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High."
"797","777 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah ibn Qudamah, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali complained, and Abu Musa came to visit him; 'Ali said to him: Did you come visiting the sick, O Abu Musa, or visiting? For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No Muslim visits a sick Muslim in the morning except seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and a harvest of Paradise is made for him; and if he visits him in the evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning, and a harvest of Paradise is made for him. And this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali with the like of these words through other channels; nor do we know of it being narrated except from 'Ali."
"798","778 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: Kisra gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he accepted from him; Qaysar gifted to him, and he accepted from him; and the kings gifted to him, and he accepted from them. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated with this wording except from 'Ali with this chain."
"799","779 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi, who is al-Sufi, narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Miqdam narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Fakhitah, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while I and al-Hasan and al-Husayn were sleeping in a blanket, or in a garment; al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to a vessel of ours and poured into the cup and brought it; al-Husayn jumped to it, and he motioned with his hand; Fatimah said: As if he is more beloved to you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He asked for water before him; and I and you and these two and this sleeping one will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"800","And among what al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah narrated from 'Ali: 780 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, he said: 'Ali was brought water and drank it standing, then said: People dislike drinking standing, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing. Then he was brought water and wiped, and said: This is the ablution of one who has not broken ablution. And 'Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, the imams narrated from him: al-A'mash, Shu'bah, Mis'ar, and others; and it has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels. This action has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he drank standing, through several channels: Ibn 'Umar, 'A'ishah, 'Imran ibn Husayn, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, Ibn 'Abbas, Umm Sulaym, 'Abdullah ibn Unays, and others narrated that he drank standing; and it was mentioned from Abu Nu'aym, and also from Mis'ar, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from al-Nazzal, from 'Ali, with the like of it. He said: Then he took some water - I think he said: and wiped his face and his hands and his feet - and said: Thus is the ablution of one who has not broken ablution."
"801","And among what al-Harith ibn Suwayd narrated from 'Ali: 801 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in the dubba' and the muzaffat. And this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels, and this chain is the best chain narrated in that regard; and it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the dubba', the hantam, and the muzaffat, through several channels: Ibn 'Umar, Jabir, Anas, Abu Sa'id, Abu Hurayrah, Buraydah, 'A'ishah, and others narrated it."
"802","And among what Husayn ibn Qabisah narrated from 'Ali: 802 - al-Husayn ibn Abi Za'idah al-Dabbagh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: 'Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from 'Ali. [No matn is stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"803","803 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' ibn 'Umaylah al-Fazari, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, he said: I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib saying: I was a man given to madhiy, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: When you see it, perform ablution; and when you see the spurting of water, perform ghusl. And we do not know of Husayn ibn Qabisah narrating from 'Ali except this hadith; nor do we know of anyone narrating this wording from 'Ali other than him."
"804","And among what Hakim ibn Sa'd narrated from 'Ali: 804 - Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muslim ibn Sallam narrated to us, from 'Imran ibn Zibyan, from Hakim ibn Sa'd, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would say: O Allah, by You I move about, and by You I assault, and by You I fight. And we do not know of these words being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; nor do we know of Hakim ibn Sa'd raising anything from 'Ali other than this hadith."
"805","And among what Sharik ibn Hanbal narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 805 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sharik ibn Hanbal, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not approach our mosque - or: the mosque - meaning garlic. And we do not know of Sharik ibn Hanbal narrating from 'Ali except this hadith; and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated from 'Umayr ibn Qumaym, from Sharik ibn Hanbal, without saying: from 'Ali."
"806","And among what Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, whose name is Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Hayyan, narrated from his father from 'Ali: 806 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi' al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, whose name is Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr: he married his daughter to me, carried me to the abode of migration, and freed Bilal with his wealth; may Allah have mercy on 'Umar: he speaks the truth even if bitter - truth has left him without friend; may Allah have mercy on 'Uthman: the angels are shy of him; may Allah have mercy on 'Ali: O Allah, turn the truth with him wherever he turns. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this chain."
"807","807 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu 'Attab narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off (a hand) for an iron egg worth twenty-one dirhams."
"808","808 - And thus Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated it to us, from Abu 'Attab, from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali. And others narrated it from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Matar, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"809","809 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar Abu Ishaq al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: I entered the mosque, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of his companions; I said: Peace be upon you. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah: twenty for me and ten for you. He said: I entered a second time and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and twenty for you. I entered a third time and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and thirty for you; I and you, O 'Ali, are equal in greeting. O 'Ali, whoever passes by a gathering and greets them, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten bad deeds, and raises him ten degrees. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this wording through this channel."
"810","810 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times. And we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali, except 'Ali ibn 'Asim."
"811","And among what Zadha n narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 811 - Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, that he drank standing, and the people looked at him and disapproved; so 'Ali said: What do you disapprove of my drinking standing? I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing."
"812","812 - And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated it to us, he said: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Maysarah, he said: I saw 'Ali drinking standing, and he saw the people looking at him, and said: If I drink standing, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing; and if I drink sitting, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking sitting."
"813","813 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"814","814 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the place of a hair not touched by water, meaning from janabah, such-and-such of the Fire will be done to him. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"815","815 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Zamin, from Zadha n, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The first prayer in which we bowed was 'Asr; I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: With this I was commanded."
"816","And among what 'Abis ibn Rabi'ah narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 816 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Asma bint 'Abis, from her father, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miscarried fetus contends with his Lord, refusing to say: Enter Paradise; it will be said to him: O miscarried one contending with his Lord, enter Paradise. He will say: Until my parents enter. It will be said: Go back and bring your parents into Paradise; so he will drag them both by their umbilical cords until he brings them into Paradise. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him; nor do we know of a path from 'Ali except this path."
"817","And among what al-Hasan ibn Sa'd narrated from his father from 'Ali: 817 - Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; and I think al-Hajjaj ibn Artah erred in its chain; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub only narrated it in a chain of his from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Rabah, from 'Uthman."
"818","818 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go on a campaign and called Ja'far, ordering him to stay behind over Madinah. He said: I will never stay behind after you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent and called me, and insisted that I stay behind before I spoke; I wept, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you weep? I said: What makes me weep are several things: Quraysh will say tomorrow: How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and forsook him; and another thing makes me weep: I wanted to expose myself to jihad in the path of Allah, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: Nor do they tread a ground enraging the disbelievers, nor attain anything from an enemy, except a righteous deed is written for them thereby; Allah does not waste the reward of the good-doers. I wanted to expose myself to reward; and another thing makes me weep: I wanted to expose myself to the bounty of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for your saying: Quraysh will say: How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and forsook him - you have in me an example: they said to me: sorcerer, soothsayer, liar. As for your saying: I expose myself to reward from Allah - are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? As for your saying: I expose myself to the bounty of Allah - here are two sacks of pepper that came to us from Yemen; sell it and enjoy it, you and Fatimah, until Allah brings you of His bounty. And this hadith is not preserved from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; and Hakim ibn Jubayr, we have already mentioned his weakness in another place."
"819","And among what Abu al-Janub narrated from 'Ali: 819 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Janub narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Talhah and al-Zubayr are my two neighbors in Paradise. And we do not know of these words being narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel from 'Ali with this chain."
"820","820 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abu Sa'id said: I asked a man of his people about his name, and al-Nadr said: Abu al-Janub narrated to us, he said: 'Ali narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man of the people of al-'Aliyah came upon us and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of the severest thing in this religion and the gentlest. He said: The gentlest is the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; and the severest, O brother of al-'Aliyah, is trustworthiness: there is no religion for one with no trustworthiness, no prayer for him and no zakah for him. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires wealth unlawfully and spends it will not be rewarded for it; and if he stores it, it will be his provision to the Fire. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires unlawful wealth and wears a jilbab, meaning a shirt, his prayer will not be accepted until he removes that jilbab from himself; Allah, blessed and exalted is He, is too generous and mighty, O brother of al-'Aliyah, to accept the deed of a man, or his prayer, while upon him is a jilbab of unlawful wealth. And we do not know of a chain for this hadith except this chain; and Abu al-Janub, we do not know of anyone raising from him except al-Nadr ibn Mansur."
"821","And among what al-Harith al-A'war ibn 'Abdullah narrated from 'Ali - al-Sha'bi from al-Harith from 'Ali: 821 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali. [No matn is stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"822","822 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Muhadir narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from 'Amir, from al-Harith, from 'Ali. [No matn is stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"823","823 - And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd al-Ayami narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from 'Amir, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, and from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cursed ten: the eater of riba and its giver, its scribe and its two witnesses, the tattooer and the tattooed, the withholder of charity, and the muhallil and the one for whom it is done."
"824","824 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver, its two witnesses and its scribe, and the one deeming lawful and the one for whom it is deemed lawful, and the tattooer and the tattooed, and the withholder of his charity. And the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Abu Salamah from Hammad."
"825","825 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The eater of riba and its giver were cursed; then he mentioned the like of it. Al-Bazzar said: This was only entered into the Musnad because he said: they were cursed."
"826","807 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu 'Attab narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from his father, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off (a hand) for an iron egg worth twenty-one dirhams."
"827","808 - And thus Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated it to us, from Abu 'Attab, from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali. And others narrated it from al-Mukhtar, from Abu Matar, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"828","809 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Mukhtar Abu Ishaq al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali, he said: I entered the mosque, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of his companions; I said: Peace be upon you. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah: twenty for me and ten for you. He said: I entered a second time and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and twenty for you. I entered a third time and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings: thirty for me and thirty for you; I and you, O 'Ali, are equal in greeting. O 'Ali, whoever passes by a gathering and greets them, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten bad deeds, and raises him ten degrees. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this wording through this channel."
"829","810 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times. And we do not know of anyone narrating it from Abu Hayyan, from his father, from 'Ali, except 'Ali ibn 'Asim."
"830","And among what Zadha n narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 811 - Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, that he drank standing, and the people looked at him and disapproved; so 'Ali said: What do you disapprove of my drinking standing? I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing."
"831","812 - And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated it to us, he said: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Maysarah, he said: I saw 'Ali drinking standing, and he saw the people looking at him, and said: If I drink standing, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking standing; and if I drink sitting, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking sitting."
"832","813 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"833","814 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadha n, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the place of a hair not touched by water, meaning from janabah, such-and-such of the Fire will be done to him. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"834","815 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Zamin, from Zadha n, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The first prayer in which we bowed was 'Asr; I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: With this I was commanded."
"835","And among what 'Abis ibn Rabi'ah narrated from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: 816 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Asma bint 'Abis, from her father, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miscarried fetus contends with his Lord, refusing to say: Enter Paradise; it will be said to him: O miscarried one contending with his Lord, enter Paradise. He will say: Until my parents enter. It will be said: Go back and bring your parents into Paradise; so he will drag them both by their umbilical cords until he brings them into Paradise. And we do not know of anyone narrating this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him; nor do we know of a path from 'Ali except this path."
"836","And among what al-Hasan ibn Sa'd narrated from his father from 'Ali: 817 - Talut ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; and I think al-Hajjaj ibn Artah erred in its chain; Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub only narrated it in a chain of his from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Rabah, from 'Uthman."
"837","818 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from his father, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go on a campaign and called Ja'far, ordering him to stay behind over Madinah. He said: I will never stay behind after you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent and called me, and insisted that I stay behind before I spoke; I wept, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you weep? I said: What makes me weep are several things: Quraysh will say tomorrow: How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and forsook him; and another thing makes me weep: I wanted to expose myself to jihad in the path of Allah, for Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says: Nor do they tread a ground enraging the disbelievers, nor attain anything from an enemy, except a righteous deed is written for them thereby; Allah does not waste the reward of the good-doers. I wanted to expose myself to reward; and another thing makes me weep: I wanted to expose myself to the bounty of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for your saying: Quraysh will say: How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and forsook him - you have in me an example: they said to me: sorcerer, soothsayer, liar. As for your saying: I expose myself to reward from Allah - are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? As for your saying: I expose myself to the bounty of Allah - here are two sacks of pepper that came to us from Yemen; sell it and enjoy it, you and Fatimah, until Allah brings you of His bounty. And this hadith is not preserved from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain; and Hakim ibn Jubayr, we have already mentioned his weakness in another place."
"838","And among what Abu al-Janub narrated from 'Ali: 819 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Janub narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Talhah and al-Zubayr are my two neighbors in Paradise. And we do not know of these words being narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel from 'Ali with this chain."
"839","820 - 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abu Sa'id said: I asked a man of his people about his name, and al-Nadr said: Abu al-Janub narrated to us, he said: 'Ali narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man of the people of al-'Aliyah came upon us and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of the severest thing in this religion and the gentlest. He said: The gentlest is the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; and the severest, O brother of al-'Aliyah, is trustworthiness: there is no religion for one with no trustworthiness, no prayer for him and no zakah for him. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires wealth unlawfully and spends it will not be rewarded for it; and if he stores it, it will be his provision to the Fire. O brother of al-'Aliyah, whoever acquires unlawful wealth and wears a jilbab, meaning a shirt, his prayer will not be accepted until he removes that jilbab from himself; Allah, blessed and exalted is He, is too generous and mighty, O brother of al-'Aliyah, to accept the deed of a man, or his prayer, while upon him is a jilbab of unlawful wealth. And we do not know of a chain for this hadith except this chain; and Abu al-Janub, we do not know of anyone raising from him except al-Nadr ibn Mansur."
"840","And among what al-Harith al-A'war ibn 'Abdullah narrated from 'Ali - al-Sha'bi from al-Harith from 'Ali: 821 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali. [No matn is stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"841","822 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Muhadir narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from 'Amir, from al-Harith, from 'Ali. [No matn is stated in this report beyond the chain.]"
"842","823 - And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd al-Ayami narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from 'Amir, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, and from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he cursed ten: the eater of riba and its giver, its scribe and its two witnesses, the tattooer and the tattooed, the withholder of charity, and the muhallil and the one for whom it is done."
"843","824 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver, its two witnesses and its scribe, and the one deeming lawful and the one for whom it is deemed lawful, and the tattooer and the tattooed, and the withholder of his charity. And the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, we do not know of anyone narrating it except Abu Salamah from Hammad."
"844","825 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The eater of riba and its giver were cursed; then he mentioned the like of it. Al-Bazzar said: This was only entered into the Musnad because he said: they were cursed."
"845","826 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, with the like of it, without saying: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"846","827 - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"847","828 - And Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Layth, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The eater of riba and its giver were cursed; then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."
"848","829 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Husayn and Mughirah and Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver; then he mentioned the like of it. And more than one narrated it from Ibn 'Awn, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali; some raised it and some stopped it; nor do we know of anyone narrating it from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, except Hushaym."
"849","830 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Dawud, meaning al-Awdi, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [No matn beyond this chain is stated in this report.]"
"850","831 - And Maymun ibn al-Asbagh and 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, they said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [No matn beyond this chain is stated in this report.]"
"851","832 - Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Fudayl, meaning Ibn Marzuq, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [No matn beyond this chain is stated in this report.]"
"852","833 - And Muhammad ibn Abi Madh'ur narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal and Abu Ishaq al-Kufi narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was with him, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar came forward, and he said: These two are the leaders of the old of the people of Paradise, of the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. And the hadith of Dawud al-Awdi from al-Sha'bi, we heard it only from Ya'qub al-Dawraqi, from Ibn 'Uyaynah; and the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Ibn 'Uyaynah except Ibn Abi Maryam; and the hadith of Firas, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Firas except al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq; and the hadith of Malik ibn Mighwal and Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, we do not know of anyone narrating it from Hushaym as connected except Muhammad ibn 'Isa and Ibn Abi Madh'ur; and more than one narrated it from Malik ibn Mighwal and Abu Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, disconnected."
"853","834 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The bedding of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, on the night she was brought to me, was only a ram's skin."
"854","835 - al-Husayn ibn 'Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: I heard him mentioning it from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Layth, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: These two are the leaders of the old of the people of Paradise; and do not tell them. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the hadith of Layth except from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad from him."
"855","And among what Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrated from al-Harith from 'Ali: 836 - 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah al-A'war, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: O Muhammad, your nation will differ after you. He said: I said: What is the way out, O Jibril? He said: The Book of Allah: refuge is taken in it from every tyrant; whoever holds to it is saved, and whoever leaves it perishes; a decisive word, not jest; tongues do not wear it out, it does not become heavy from long repetition, its wonders do not end; in it is the account of what was before it, the judgment of what is among you, and the report of what will be after you. And we do not know of Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrating from al-Harith, from 'Ali, except this hadith."
"856","And among what Abu al-Bakhtari narrated from al-Harith from 'Ali: 837 - Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There will be tribulation after you; so he asked him - or he was asked - what is the way out? He said: The Book."
"857","838 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Malik ibn Su'ayr narrated to us, he said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Abi al-Mukhtar, he said: The nephew of al-Harith al-A'war narrated to us, from al-Harith al-A'war, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him - both their hadiths are close, and the wording is the wording of the nephew of al-Harith, from al-Harith al-A'war, from 'Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be tribulation. He said: I said: What is the way out of it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Book of Allah: in it is the account of what was before you, the report of what is after you, and the judgment of what is among you; it is the criterion, not jest; whoever is opposed by a tyrant, Allah breaks him; whoever seeks guidance in other than it, Allah misguides him; it is the firm rope of Allah, the Wise Remembrance, and the Straight Path, which desires do not swerve, the scholars are not sated of it, it does not wear out from repetition, its wonders do not end; and it is that when the jinn heard it, they did not cease to say: We heard a wondrous Qur'an; whoever speaks by it is truthful, whoever acts by it is rewarded, whoever judges by it is just, whoever calls to it is guided to a straight path, and whoever holds to it is guided to a straight path. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated except from 'Ali; nor do we know of anyone narrating it from 'Ali except al-Harith."
"858","And among what Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated from al-Harith from 'Ali: 839 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah, narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If I were to appoint anyone of my nation over them without consultation among them, I would appoint over them Ibn Umm 'Abd."
"859","840 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"860","841 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged debt before bequest, while you recite: After a bequest bequeathed or a debt; and he judged that full brothers from the same mother inherit to the exclusion of half-brothers by the father."
"861","842 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has pardoned you the charity on horses and slaves. And this hadith, its narration from Abu Ishaq differs: more than one narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim, from 'Ali; and more than one narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."
"862","843 - Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had a hundred uqiyyahs and gave ten uqiyyahs in charity of it; and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had a hundred dinars and gave ten dinars in charity of it; and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had ten dinars and gave a dinar in charity of it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are equal in reward, each of you giving a tenth of his wealth in charity. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from 'Ali, from him, peace be upon him, with this chain."
"863","844 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam, meaning Ibn Sulaym, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of people are those upon whom the Hour comes while alive, and those who take graves as mosques, and those who testify with testimony before they are asked for it. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel with this chain."
"864","845 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr, meaning 'Abdullah ibn Numayr, narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to recite the Qur'an while bowing or prostrating. And this hadith has been narrated from 'Ali through other channels; so we mentioned it from the hadith of Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."
"865","846 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra' narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no zakah in ninety and a hundred - meaning of silver - except what its owner wishes; when it reaches two hundred, in it are five dirhams; when it increases, accordingly. And this hadith, al-A'mash and Abu 'Awanah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn Damrah, from 'Ali; and al-Hajjaj said: from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali."
"866","847 - Abu Kurayb and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the fear prayer two rak'ahs, except Maghrib three; and I prayed with him traveling two rak'ahs, except Maghrib three. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain from the narration of 'Ali from him."
"867","848 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family used to bathe from one vessel, and neither of them would bathe with the leftover of the other. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel."
"868","849 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought protection for a sick person, he would say: Remove the harm, Lord of people, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing leaving no sickness. And we do not know of this hadith being narrated from 'Ali except through this channel."
"869","850 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: From every part of the night the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr: its beginning, its middle, and its end; and he fixed his witr at the end of the night."
"870","851 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a man of my companions is sought as a stray is sought, and is not found."
"871","852 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A Muslim owes a Muslim six acts of kindness: he greets him when he meets him, visits him when he is sick, accepts his invitation when he invites him, attends his funeral when he dies, and gives him sincere advice in his absence."" Abu Bakr said: And one of them slipped my mind."
"872","853 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with nine surahs of the Mufassal: in the first rak'ah: {Rivalry in increase distracted you}, {Indeed We sent it down in the Night of Decree}, and {When the earth is shaken}; in the second rak'ah: {By time}, {When the help of Allah comes and the conquest}, and {Indeed We gave you al-Kawthar}; and in the third rak'ah: {Say: O disbelievers}, {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}. Abu Bakr said: These hadiths which Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali — we do not know anyone who narrated them except Ali."
"873","854 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If I were to appoint anyone in authority without consultation, I would appoint Ibn Umm Abd."""
"874","855 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the red saddle cloth. This hadith was narrated by others besides Abu Salamah, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Ali."
"875","856 - Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""I love for you what I love for myself: do not prompt the imam during prayer, do not fiddle with pebbles during prayer, do not crack your fingers during prayer, do not turn to your right nor to your left during prayer, and do not spread your forearms in prayer as the beast spreads."" This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route, and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq and Isra'il narrated it from Abu Ishaq."
"876","857 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: It is of the Sunnah that a man leads with two men behind him and a woman behind them. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route."
"877","858 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr at the time of the iqamah. Abu Bakr said: I saw this in my book from Abu Amir, from Isra'il, but I had memorized it from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq."
"878","859 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr at the time of the adhan and pray the two rak'ahs at the time of the iqamah."
"879","860 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer at sunrise until it has risen, at sunset until it has set, and at midday until the sun has declined. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route, and none narrated it from Ali except al-Harith."
"880","861 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who pays it, the one who marries a woman to make her lawful for her former husband, and the one for whom that is done."
"881","862 - Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr al-Mulla'i narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb, the seller of saddle blankets, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah does not love the ignorant old man, nor the unjust rich man, nor the scheming poor man."" This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route, and we do not recall it from other than Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and this Shu'ayb is not well known."
"882","863 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hilal, the freed slave of Rabi'ah, narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""Whoever owns provisions and a mount that can carry him, yet does not perform Hajj to the House of Allah — it will not harm him whether he dies as a Jew or as a Christian."" This hadith we do not know to have any chain from Ali except this chain; Hilal is a Basran from whom a number of Basrans narrated — Affan, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and others — and we do not know it narrated from Ali except through this route."
"883","864 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest."" This hadith was narrated by Hammad from al-Hajjaj, and we do not know anyone else who narrated it; and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated it from his father, from al-Harith, from Ali."
"884","865 - Muhammad ibn al-Mustanir al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"885","866 - al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Sa'ad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am to be taken (in death), and I have left among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my household; you will never go astray after them, and the Hour will not come until the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are sought like a lost animal is sought and are not found."""
"886","867 - al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Sa'ad narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning the Khawarij: A people at the end of time who recite the Qur'an which will not pass their throats; they will exit the religion as the arrow exits the target."
"887","868 - al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Sa'ad narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the fear prayer: he commanded the people to take up their weapons upon them; one group stood behind them facing the enemy, and another group came and prayed with him — he prayed one rak'ah with them, then they went to the group that had not prayed, and the group that had not prayed with him came and stood behind him, and he prayed one rak'ah with them and two prostrations, then greeted them; when he greeted, those who had been facing the enemy stood, all said takbir, bowed one rak'ah and performed two prostrations after he had greeted."
"888","Among what Tha'labah ibn Yazid al-Himmani narrated from Ali — Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Tha'labah. 869 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tha'labah al-Himmani, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."" This hadith was narrated from al-A'mash by Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid and others."
"889","870 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Artah, narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tha'labah, from Ali, he said: He forbade the gold ring and the saddle cloth. This hadith has been narrated from Ali through more than one route, and the hadith of Habib was narrated from him only by al-Hajjaj."
"890","871 - Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ajlah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tha'labah ibn Yazid, from his father — thus he said, and I think it is a mistake; rather it is from Ali — he said: I heard Ali say upon the pulpit: By Allah, the covenant of the unlettered Prophet to me is that the ummah will betray me. This hadith was narrated by more than one from Habib, from Tha'labah, from Ali: Fitr ibn Khalifah and others."
"891","872 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Tha'labah ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) — or Yazid ibn Tha'labah, from Ali — he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to level every protruding grave and efface every idol, so I did; then I came to him and he said: Did you do it? I said: Yes."
"892","873 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tha'labah ibn Yazid al-Himmani, he said: Ali said: By the One who split the grain and created the soul, this (beard) will surely be dyed from this (head) — his beard from his head — so who will restrain the most wretched of them? Abdullah ibn Subay' said: By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, if a man did that we would wipe out his kin. He said: I adjure you by Allah not to kill anyone other than my killer because of me. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, will you not appoint a successor over us? He said: No, but I leave you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you. He said: What will you say to your Lord when you come to Him, having left us neglected? He said: I will say: You entrusted me with them as long as You willed, then You took me and left them in Your care."
"893","Among what Kulayb Abu Asim narrated from Ali. 874 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: The gatherings of the people were the mosques until they returned from Siffin and disavowed the arbitration; then people took matters lightly and sat in the streets exchanging news. While we were sitting with Ali as he spoke about some affair of the people, a man stood over him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, permit me to speak. He said: He was distracted by what he was engaged in of the people's affair. He said: So we took the man, seated him with us and said: What is this you wish to ask the Commander of the Faithful about? He said: I was in Umrah and entered upon the Mother of the Believers Aishah, and she said: Who are these who came out before you, called Harura'? I said: A people who went out to a land near us called Harura'. He said: Did you witness their destruction? Asim said: I do not know what the man said, yes or no. Aishah said: Indeed Ibn Abi Talib, if he wished, could tell you their account — so I came to ask him about that. When Ali finished what he was engaged in, he said: Where is the man who sought permission? He said: He stood and related to him the same as he had related to us. He said: Ali exclaimed tahlil and takbir and said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with none but Aishah present, and he said: How will you be, O son of Abu Talib, with such-and-such people? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then he repeated it and I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A people who come out from the east, reciting the Qur'an which does not pass their throats; they exit the religion as the arrow exits the target; among them is a man with a defective arm, as if his hand were a breast. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, did I not tell you that he was among them, then you came to me and said: He is not among them, then you brought him to me dragging him? They said: Yes. Then Ali exclaimed tahlil and takbir."
"894","875 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Maslamah informed us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"895","876 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, he said: Ali was in the mosque — I think he said: the mosque of Kufah — and heard a loud clamour, and asked: Who are these? They said: People reciting the Qur'an. He said: Indeed, they were the most beloved of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim ibn Kulayb except Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi; this Abu Ya'qub is a well-known man from whom Ubaydullah ibn Musa, Husayn ibn al-Hasan and others narrated."
"896","Among what Jurayy ibn Kulayb — a man of Basrah — narrated from Ali. 877 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, a man of them, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or ear. He said: I mentioned it to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and he said: Yes; the break is half or more."
"897","878 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Sadusi, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing an animal with a mutilated ear or horn. Qatadah said: I said to Sa'id: What is adba'? He said: Half or more."
"898","879 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Sadusi, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan forbidding mut'ah, and Ali ibn Abi Talib commanding it; so I came to Ali and said: There is indeed evil between you two — you command it while Uthman forbids it. He said: Between us there is nothing but good, but the best of us is the most adherent of us to this religion. We do not know Qatadah narrated from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, from Ali, except these two hadiths."
"899","Among what Abdullah ibn Ya'la narrated from Ali. 880 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ya'la narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali say — he said: I said: Did you yourself hear from Ali? He said: Yes, and I was present with him at Siffin — that Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) came complaining to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about work, and he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you: glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. We do not know Abdullah ibn Ya'la narrated from Ali except this hadith."
"900","Among what Abdullah ibn Nujayy narrated from Ali. 881 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Mudrik al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, from Ali, he said: I had a standing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that no one had: I would come to him every dawn and greet him until he cleared his throat, then I would leave for my family. One day I came, greeted him and said: Peace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Wait, O Abu al-Hasan, until I come out to you. When he came out to me I said: O Prophet of Allah, you never refrained from speaking to me before, yet tonight you spoke to me only now. He said: I heard movement in the room and said: Who is this? He said: I am Jibril. I said: Enter. He said: No — come out to me. When I went out to him he said: In your house is something no angel enters while it remains in it. He said: I do not know of it, O Jibril. He said: Go and look. So I opened the door and found nothing in it except a puppy with which al-Hasan was playing. I said: I found nothing but a puppy. He said: He will never enter it while one of three remains in it: a dog, one in a state of janabah, or an image of a living being. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Shurahbil except Muhammad ibn Ubayd."
"901","882 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah narrating from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is one in janabah, a dog, or an image."
"902","883 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Zur'ah narrating from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"903","884 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Umarah, meaning Ibn al-Qa'qa', narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, he said: I had an hour of the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I would come to him, and if he was praying he would clear his throat, otherwise he would admit me."
"904","885 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nujayy narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard a sound in the house, so I went out and there was Jibril, peace be upon him. I said: What prevented you from entering? He said: The angel does not enter a house in which there is a dog, an image, or one in janabah; and in the house was a puppy with which al-Hasan ibn Ali was playing."
"905","886 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Mudrik al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from his father, that he travelled with Ali and was the keeper of his water for purification. When he came parallel to Nineveh while heading to Siffin, Ali called out: Patience, O Abu Abdullah. I said: What is it, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah one day with his eyes overflowing, and I said: O Prophet of Allah, has someone angered you — what is wrong with your eyes overflowing? He said: Rather Jibril just left me and told me that al-Husayn will be killed at the bank of the Euphrates. He said: Would you like me to let you smell some of its soil? He said: I said: Yes. He said: He stretched his hand and took a handful of soil, and I could not hold back my eyes from overflowing. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route with this chain. Ahmad said: Abdullah ibn Nujayy and his father both heard from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"906","887 - al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Asbat narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Are you not pleased to be the mistress of the women of Paradise, and your two sons the masters of the youth of Paradise?"
"907","Among what Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi narrated from Ali. 888 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in his right hand and silk in his left and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah, lawful for its females."
"908","889 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"909","890 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route with this chain."
"910","891 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr, from Ali, he said: A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it pleased him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, if we bred donkeys with our horses they would produce the like of this. He said: Only those who lack understanding do that."
"911","892 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi al-Saghani narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid and Ibn Hubayrah, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing leading them in prayer when he left, then came with his head dripping water, and said: I stood to lead you, then remembered that I was in janabah and had not bathed, so I left and bathed; whoever among you experiences the like of what befell me, or finds rumbling in his stomach, let him leave and bathe or perform ablution. This hadith we do not recall to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"912","Among what Ujayr Abu Nafi' ibn Umayr narrated from Ali. 893 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Hadi, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Ujayr, from his father, from Ali, he said: Zayd ibn Harithah went out to Makkah and brought the daughter of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Ja'far ibn Abi Talib said: I will take her; I have more right to her — she is my cousin's daughter, and her maternal aunt is with me, and the maternal aunt is a mother. Ali said: Rather I have more right to her than you both — she is my cousin's daughter, and with me is the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who has more right to her; and I raised my voice so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear my argument before he came out. Zayd said: Rather I have more right to her — I went out to her, travelled and brought her. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: What is the matter with you? They repeated to him the like of their words, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall judge between you in this and in other matters. Ali said: When he said 'and in other matters' I said: The Qur'an was revealed about our raising our voices. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you — to Zayd — you are my freedman and theirs; he said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. And as for you, O Ja'far, you resemble me in appearance and character, and you are of my tree from which I am; he said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. And as for you, O Ali, you are my chosen one and my trustee; he said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. And as for the girl, I judge her for Ja'far, to be with her maternal aunt — for the maternal aunt is a mother. He said: We have submitted, O Messenger of Allah. We do not know Ujayr Abu Nafi' narrated from Ali except this hadith, nor do we know for it a route from Nafi', from his father, from Ali, except through this route."
"913","Among what Shabath ibn Rib'i narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib. 894 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Hadi, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Shabath ibn Rib'i, from Ali, he said: Captives were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Ali and Fatimah went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is the matter with you two? Ali said to him: O Messenger of Allah, work has become hard for us and we wanted you to give us a servant to shield us from work. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you two to what is better for you than red camels? Ali said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Takbirs, tasbihs and tahmids, one hundred when you wish to sleep, so you spend the night upon a thousand good deeds. Ali said: It never escaped me since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except on the night of Siffin, for I forgot it until I remembered it at the end of the night and said it. Abu Bakr said: This Shabath ibn Rib'i — we do not know him to narrate from Ali except this hadith, nor do we know for him a route from Ali except this route."
"914","Among what Abu al-Khalil narrated from Ali. 895 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Sufyan. And Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali, he said: I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his two parents though they were polytheists, so I said: You seek forgiveness for your parents though they are polytheists? He said: Did Ibrahim not seek forgiveness for his father? I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whereupon was revealed: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the polytheists} to the end of the verse. These words we do not know anyone narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali, nor do we know for it from Ali a chain other than this chain."
"915","Among what Abu Razin narrated from Ali. 896 - Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Razin, from his father, from Ali, he said: I said to al-Abbas: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the custodianship of the Ka'bah for us, so he asked him and he said: I give you the watering (siqayah), which will provide for you without you providing for it. He said: I said to al-Abbas: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to employ you over the charities, and he said: I would never employ you over the filth of people's sins. This hadith we do not know to have a chain from Ali except this chain."
"916","Among what Abdullah ibn Mulayl narrated from Ali. 897 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, they said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Kathir, the seller of date pits, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mulayl say: I heard Ali say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that there was no prophet but was given seven noble companions and ministers, and I was given fourteen: Hamzah, Ja'far, Ali, Hasan, Husayn, Abu Bakr, Umar, Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Abu Dharr, al-Miqdad, Hudhayfah, Ammar, Salman and Bilal. These words we do not know anyone narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ali, nor do we know for it a chain from Ali except this chain."
"917","Among what Tariq ibn Ziyad narrated from Ali. 898 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la, from Tariq ibn Ziyad, he said: When Ali killed the people of al-Nahr, he said: Search, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will come out speaking the word of truth which will not pass their throats; they are the worst of people — so search for him. We searched and found him, so we fell in prostration and Ali fell prostrate with us. We do not know Tariq ibn Ziyad narrated from Ali except this hadith."
"918","Among what al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah narrated from Ali. 899 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya Abu Ishaq al-Darir al-Mu'allim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Qudamah ibn Wabarah, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Baqi', meaning Baqi' al-Gharqad, on a rainy day, when a woman passed on a donkey with a donkey-driver; she passed through a hollow in the ground and fell, so he turned his face away from her. They said: O Messenger of Allah, she is wearing trousers. He said: O Allah, forgive the trouser-wearing women of my ummah. These words we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain; this Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya was not corroborated in this hadith and is rejected in hadith."
"919","900 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hammad Abu al-Jahm narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah al-Thumali narrated to us, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, set prices for us. He said: High prices and low prices are in Allah's hand; I wish to meet my Lord with none demanding of me an injustice I did to him. These words have been narrated with similar wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other routes, but we do not know it narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route with this chain; as for al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, most of his hadiths from Ali are narrated by no one else."
"920","Among what Abu Mu'min narrated from Ali. 901 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'min narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day the Haruriyyah were killed, while I was with my master, and he said: Look, for among them is a man one of whose hands is like a woman's breast; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me that I am the one concerned with him. They turned over the slain and did not find him, and said: Seven men under the palm trees we have not yet turned over. He said: Woe to you, look. Abu Mu'min said: I saw two ropes on his legs with which they dragged him until they cast him before him; then Ali fell prostrate and said: Rejoice — your slain are in Paradise and their slain are in the Fire. We do not know Abu Mu'min narrated from Ali except this hadith."
"921","Among what Burayd ibn Asram narrated from Ali. 902 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Utbah — or Utaybah — narrating from Burayd ibn Asram, he said: I heard Ali say: A man of the people of al-Suffah died leaving a dinar and a dirham, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands — pray over your companion. We do not know Burayd ibn Asram narrated from Ali except this hadith, nor did any narrate it from him except Utbah — or Utaybah — and we do not know it narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"922","Among what Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated from Ali. 903 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i. And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash say: I heard Ali delivering a sermon, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire. This hadith was narrated by more than one from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Ali, and it was also narrated from Ali through another route with different wording."
"923","904 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No servant believes until he believes in four: that he testifies there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah sent with the truth, believes in resurrection after death, and believes in the Decree."
"924","905 - Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Ali, he said: Quraysh gathered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our slaves have joined you, and there has entered with you in this affair those unworthy of it — return them to us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until anger was seen in his face, then said: Desist, O company of Quraysh, or Allah will send a man from among you whose heart Allah has tested with faith, who will strike your necks over religion. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr? He said: No. It was said: Umar? He said: No, but it is the mender of the sandal who is in the room. Ali said: I was the mender of the sandal. Ali said: People then quoted that from Ali, and he said: Indeed I heard him say: Do not lie about me, for whoever deliberately lies about me, let him enter the Fire. This hadith was narrated by Sharik from Mansur, and Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Mansur; we do not know it narrated from Ali except through the hadith of Rib'i from him (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"925","Among what Abu Hanash narrated from Ali. 906 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hanash ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men set out for a need of theirs and sheltered by a mountain, which collapsed upon them. They said — O people, meaning some to others — reflect upon your best deeds and supplicate Allah with them; perhaps Allah will relieve you. One of them said: O Allah, he had a woman friend to whom he would frequently go until he attained his need from her; she said: I remind you of Allah not to take from me what Allah has forbidden to you. So he said: I am more deserving to fear — so I left her out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure; if You know that, relieve us. He said: The mountain cracked open for them until they hoped to exit, but could not get out. The second said: O Allah, there were hirelings working a job — I think he said — each took his wage, while one left his wage claiming his wage was greater than his companions' wages; so I set aside his wage from my wealth until it became wealth and livestock. He came to me after becoming needy and old and said: I remind you of Allah concerning my wage, for I am in greatest need of it. So I set out above a house and showed him what Allah had grown of his wage in wealth and livestock in the open land, meaning in the deserts, and said: This is yours. He said: Why do you mock me, may Allah set you right? I wanted less than this yet you refused me. So I handed it to him — O Lord — out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure; if You know that, relieve us. The mountain cracked open for them but they could not exit. The third said: O Lord, I had two elderly, needy parents with no servant, shepherd or guardian but me; I grazed for them by day and returned to them by night. Pasture grew distant so I went far with the livestock, and came to them — meaning one night — after part of the night had passed and they had slept. So I milked — meaning into the vessel — then sat by their heads with the vessel, disliking to wake them, until they would wake of themselves. O Allah, if You know I did that out of fear of You and seeking Your pleasure, relieve us. The mountain cracked open and they exited. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except with this chain; more than one narrated it from Hanash, from his father, from Ali, as a stopped report, while Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man and Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah raised it from Hanash, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"926","Among what Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl narrated from Ali. 907 - Umar ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are its possessor of two horns — so do not follow one glance with another, for the first is for you. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except with this chain; this Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl we do not know to have narrated from Ali except this hadith, nor did any narrate it from him except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, and we do not know for it a chain except this chain."
"927","Among what Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam narrated from Ali. 908 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir, meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, he said: Nafi' ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, that Ali narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood once, then did not stand — meaning for the funeral."
"928","909 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Yusuf ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from his father, that he attended a funeral at Kufah with Ali; Ali passed by the people while they were standing and gestured to them to sit, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — I think he said — used to stand, then sat. This hadith was narrated by Ibn Jurayj from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Yusuf ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"929","910 - Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Yusuf ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from his father, from Ali, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, with something similar. We do not know Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam narrated with a chain from Ali except this hadith from Ali, though it has been narrated from Ali through another route."
"930","Among what Abu Hayyaj al-Asadi narrated from Ali. 911 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud and Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, they said: Qays narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abi al-Hayyaj, from his father, he said: Ali said to me: Shall I not send you upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me upon: that I pass by no grave except I level it, and the effacing of statues. This hadith was narrated by others besides Qays from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abi al-Hayyaj, from his father, from Ali. We do not know anyone who said: from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Abi al-Hayyaj, from his father, except Qays."
"931","Among what Abu al-Bakhtari narrated from Ali. 912 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me while I am young to judge among them, and I do not know what judging is. So he struck my chest with his hand and said: O Allah, guide his heart and make his tongue firm. He said: By the One who split the grain, I never doubted after that in judging between two men. This hadith was narrated by Shu'bah from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: One who heard Ali narrated to me, saying; Abu al-Bakhtari's hearing from Ali is not sound, but we mentioned of his hadith to show that he narrated from Ali though he did not hear from Ali."
"932","913 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, they said: Mansur ibn Wardan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: When this verse was revealed: {To Allah is owed Hajj of the House by whoever can find a way to it}, they said to the Messenger: Every year? He was silent, then they said: Every year? He said: No — had I said yes it would have become obligatory. So Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if disclosed to you, would displease you}. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali except through this route with this chain; we already mentioned concerning Abu al-Bakhtari that he did not hear from Ali."
"933","Among what Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ali. 914 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: My father was over an affair of Makkah in Uthman's time; Uthman came to Makkah and he met him at Qudayd. The people of the water hunted partridges and cooked them with water and salt, making them broth for tharid; it was served to Uthman and his companions, who refrained when they saw it. Uthman said: It is game they hunted without our ordering them; lawful people hunted it and fed us — what is wrong with it? Who says this? Some said: Ali. So he sent for him and he came — as if I see him as he came brushing tree leaves off his hands. Uthman said to him: Game we did not hunt nor ordered hunted; lawful people hunted it and fed us — what is wrong with it? Ali said: I adjure by Allah any man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a leg of wild donkey — or its hind part — was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are a people in ihram, so feed it to those not in ihram. Twelve men of the Prophet's Companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified. Then he said: I adjure by Allah any man who witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when ostrich eggs were brought and he said: We are in ihram, so feed it to those not in ihram. Fewer than that number testified. So Uthman drew his leg back from the food, and the people of the water ate that food. This hadith is among the finest chains narrated from Ali on this topic."
"934","915 - Hilal ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it; the fasting one has two joys — when he breaks his fast and when he meets his Lord. By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, the breath of the fasting one's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this route with this chain."
"935","Among what Kurdus ibn Amr narrated from Ali. 916 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah narrated to us, he said: I heard Kurdus ibn Amr say: I heard a man of the people of Badr — Shu'bah said: I think him Ali ibn Abi Talib — say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you to recite the Mufassal in portions is dearer to me than so many chapters. Shu'bah said: I said to Abd al-Malik: Which Mufassal? He said: The narratives (al-Qasas). We do not know this Kurdus ibn Amr narrated from Ali except this hadith."
"936","Among what Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated from Ali. 917 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali."
"937","918 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn — I think — from his father, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing qassi and saffron-dyed garments, gold rings, and reciting the Qur'an while bowing."
"938","919 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, that Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me gold rings, saffron-dyed garments, and reciting while bowing or prostrating."
"939","920 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali."
"940","921 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam — Sa'id ibn al-Hakam — narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold rings, wearing qassi and saffron-dyed garments, and reciting in bowing and prostration — and he does not say 'he forbade you.' We do not know Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn except this hadith, nor al-Zuhri from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn except this hadith."
"941","922 - Muhammad ibn Miskin and al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated except Yahya ibn Hassan from Sulayman ibn Bilal, nor do we know it narrated from Ali except through this route with this chain."
"942","Among what Yazid ibn Bilal narrated from Ali. 923 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from his freedman Yazid ibn Bilal, he said: I saw Ali urinate, then wash his private part, perform ablution three times, wipe his head, take a handful of water and do thus with it, and wipe over his khuffs, and say: Such was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"943","924 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bilal, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eight rak'ahs at night, and when dawn approached he would perform witr with three rak'ahs; when dawn broke he would pray two rak'ahs before Fajr."
"944","925 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bilal, he said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me that none wash him but me, for none sees my nakedness but his eyes are blinded. Ali said: Al-Abbas and Usamah would hand me water from behind the curtain."
"945","926 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Kaysan Abu Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bilal, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would alternate between his feet, standing on each foot, until was revealed: {We did not send down the Qur'an upon you to distress you}. The hadiths of Yazid ibn Bilal from Ali we know to have no routes except through the hadith of Kaysan Abu Umar."
"946","Among what Fadal ibn Abi Fadalah narrated from Ali. 927 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Fadal ibn Abi Fadalah al-Ansari, he said: I went out with my father visiting Ali while he was ill, and my father said to him: What keeps you in this dwelling — if you perished here none but the bedouins of Juhaynah would take charge of you; if you entered Madinah you would be among your companions, and if what you fear befalls you, your companions would take charge of you. Abu Fadalah was of the people of Badr. Ali said to him: I shall not die of this illness of mine or this pain; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me that I shall not die until — I think he said — I am struck, or until this is dyed from this — meaning his head — then Abu Fadalah was killed with him at Siffin. We do not know Fadal ibn Abi Fadalah narrated from Ali except this hadith."
"947","Usayr ibn Safwan from Ali — Ali's praise of Abu Bakr. 928 - Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Usayr ibn Safwan, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) died, they covered him with a cloth; Madinah shook with weeping, and people were stunned as on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken. Ali ibn Abi Talib came hastening, saying 'to Allah we belong,' repeating: Today the caliphate of prophethood has ended — until he stood at the door of the house in which Abu Bakr lay and said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr. You were the foremost of the people in Islam, the purest of them in faith, the strongest in certainty, the most fearful of Allah, the greatest in sufficiency, the most protective of His Messenger, the most devoted to Islam, the most trustworthy toward his companions, the best in companionship, the most excellent in virtues, the most abundant in precedence, the highest in rank, the nearest to his Messenger, the most resembling him in guidance, character and demeanour, the most firmly trusted by him, the noblest in station, the dearest to him. May Allah reward you on behalf of Islam, His Messenger and the Muslims with good. You believed the Messenger of Allah when people disbelieved him, so He named you in His Book 'Siddiq,' saying: {He who came with the truth} — Muhammad — {and believed in it} — Abu Bakr. You consoled him when they were miserly, stood with him when they sat back from him, accompanied him in hardship with the noblest companionship; the one upon whom tranquillity was sent down, his companion in the Hijrah and in places of distress. You succeeded him over his ummah with the finest succession when people apostatized; you upheld Allah's religion with an upholding no caliph of a prophet ever did. You were strong when his companions were weak, rose when they faltered, adhered to his Messenger's ways despite the hypocrites and to the rage of the disbelievers. You managed the affair when they failed, by Allah's light when they halted. You were the highest of them above, the fewest in speech, the soundest in words, the longest in silence, the most eloquent in speech. You were the greatest of them in judgment, the bravest in heart, the strongest in certainty, the best in deed, the most knowledgeable of affairs. You were to religion its leader, and to the believers a merciful father when they became dependents upon you — you bore the burdens they were too weak for, preserved what they neglected, tended what they disregarded, and were patient when they panicked. You attained the traces of what they sought, and through you they gained what they had not reckoned. You were upon the disbelievers a pouring torment, and to the Muslims rain and fertility. You were fashioned with its richness, dignified with its sanctuary, carried off its excellences and secured its precedences. Your proof never diminished, your heart never swerved, your insight never weakened, your soul never cowered. You were like the mountain which storms do not move and tempests do not remove. You were as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most gracious of people to him in companionship and wealth; and as he said: Weak in your body, strong in Allah's affair, humble, great among the Muslims, eminent on earth. None had in you a source of criticism, nor for any speaker a point of blame, nor in you any greed, nor with you any leniency toward anyone. The weak and lowly with you was strong until you took for him his right; the strong and mighty with you was lowly and weak until the right was taken from him; near and far were with you in that alike. Your concern was truth, honesty and gentleness. Your word — then you departed with the path laid out, religion straightened through you, faith strengthened, and Allah's command manifest though the disbelievers dislike it. By Allah, you raced far ahead and wearied those after you with severe weariness; you won Paradise. Your loss was great in heaven, and your calamity shook mankind. To Allah we belong and to Him we return. We are pleased with Allah's decree and submit to Allah's command. The Muslims will never after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be afflicted with the like of you ever. You were to religion a support and cave, to the Muslims a fortress, refuge and comfort, and upon the hypocrites harshness and rage. May Allah join you to your Prophet, not deprive us of your reward, nor lead us astray after you. He said: People fell silent until he finished his speech, then the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept and said: You spoke truth, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"948","Musnad Talhah ibn Ubaydullah (may Allah be pleased with him). Beginning of the tenth part — first hadith of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. Among what Abu Hurayrah narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 929 - Abu Abdullah ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Azdi al-Basri, known as al-Bazzar, narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that two men were brethren; one was martyred and the second remained after the martyr a year. Talhah said: I saw the latter of the two men enter Paradise before the martyr, so I told people of that and it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Did he not fast Ramadan after him and pray after him six thousand and one hundred rak'ahs — meaning the prayer of the year. Abu Bakr said: This hadith was narrated by more than one from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah; and Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Talhah. We mentioned it from Ziyad because he connected it, narrating it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, may Allah have mercy on him. More than one corroborated Ziyad in his narration."
"949","Among what Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated from Talhah. 930 - Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Buhayr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say to Talhah, may Allah have mercy on them: Why do I see you gloomy since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died — is it perhaps your cousin's rule over you? He said: No, by Allah — and I am the worthiest of you not to do so. He said: What is wrong with you? He said: I heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a word no man says at death but finds relief with it when it leaves his body. Umar said: I know it. He said: What is it? He said: The word he said to his uncle — there is no god but Allah. Abu Bakr said: We do not know Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated from Talhah except this hadith, nor did any narrate it from Mujalid except Abdullah ibn Numayr."
"950","Among what Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated from Talhah. 931 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, from his father, he said: We were with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah while in ihram, and a bird was gifted to him while Talhah was asleep; some of us ate and some refrained. When Talhah awoke he was told, and he approved those who ate it and said: We ate it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr said: This hadith was narrated by more than one without perfecting its chain; we do not know anyone who connected it and perfected its chain except Ibn Jurayj from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir. We do not know Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated from Talhah except this hadith, nor do we know this wording narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route."
"951","Among what Malik ibn Abi Amir narrated from Talhah. 932 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Waddah narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Malik ibn Abi Amir, he said: I was with Talhah ibn Ubaydullah when a man entered upon him and said: O Abu Muhammad, by Allah we do not know whether this Yemeni knows the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than you, or he says about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say — meaning Abu Hurayrah. Talhah ibn Ubaydullah said: By Allah, we do not doubt he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what we did not hear, and knew what we did not know. We were wealthy people with houses and families; we would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the two ends of the day, while he was a poor man with neither wealth nor family — his hand was but with the Messenger's hand, circling with him wherever he turned. We do not doubt he knew what we did not know and heard what we did not hear; and we never found anyone of good saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. This hadith we do not know to have from Talhah a chain except this chain, nor do we know anyone narrated these words about Abu Hurayrah except Talhah."
"952","933 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, he said: My uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik informed me, from his father, that he heard Talhah ibn Ubaydullah say: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we heard his murmur without knowing what he said. He asked him about Islam, and he said: Five prayers in the day and night. He said: Is there aught else upon me? He said: No. He asked him about fasting, and he said: The month of Ramadan. He said: Is there aught else upon me? He said: No. He mentioned zakah, and he said: Is there aught else upon me? He said: No. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall neither add to them nor subtract. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has prospered if truthful. Abu Bakr said: We do not know Malik ibn Abi Amir narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah except these two hadiths, nor is this account narrated from Talhah except with this chain; it has been narrated from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"953","Among what Sa'da al-Murriyyah, wife of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, narrated. 934 - Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Yahya ibn Talhah, from Sa'da al-Murriyyah, wife of Talhah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, passed by Talhah when Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, was made caliph, and said: I see you gloomy — perhaps you dislike your cousin's rule. He said: No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say a word I did not ask him about until he died. He said: I know a word no servant says at his death but it is a light in his record, and his soul and body find rest with it at death. Umar said: I know it — it is 'there is no god but Allah,' the word he wanted his uncle to say. He said: I see it to be none but it. Abu Bakr said: This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Mis'ar with this chain except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sukkari, nor do we know anyone narrated from him except Harun ibn Ishaq; it has been narrated from Talhah through other routes, so we sufficed with Mis'ar's hadith."
"954","Among what al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 935 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, keeper of al-Sabiri, narrated to us, he said: Ubays ibn Marhum narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: I accompanied Talhah ibn Ubaydullah and Sa'd, and heard neither narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — except Talhah, for I heard him narrate about the day of Uhud. Abu Bakr said: This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Sa'ib except Muhammad ibn Yusuf; this Muhammad ibn Yusuf is the nephew of al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid."
"955","Among what Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 936 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Amiri narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Sabrah, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hadi, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the road to Makkah: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh — the most tender to a child and the most caring toward a husband. Abu Bakr said: We do not know Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated from Talhah except this hadith, nor do we know these words narrated from Talhah except with this chain, through this route; this Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah is lenient in hadith."
"956","Among what Musa ibn Talhah narrated from his father Talhah. 937 - Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: I passed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among palms and saw people atop the palms pollinating. He said: What are they doing? He said: They take from the male and place in the female. He said: I do not think this avails aught. That reached them and they abandoned it, so it became poor dates; then he said: You know better what benefits you in your worldly life; I but spoke to you a conjecture I conjectured — but what I tell you that Allah, mighty and majestic, said, I shall never lie about Allah, blessed and exalted."
"957","938 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith was narrated from Simak by Isra'il, Asbat ibn Nasr and more than one; we do not know it narrated from Talhah except through this route with this chain. It was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by a group, among them: Anas, Aishah, Rafi' ibn Khadij, Jabir ibn Abdullah and Yasir ibn Amr."
"958","939 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Simak narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place before you the like of a saddle's rear, whoever passes before you will not harm you. This hadith was also narrated from Simak by Isra'il, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father; we sufficed with Umar ibn Ubayd. It has been narrated in this chapter from Abu Dharr, Abu Hurayrah, Anas ibn Malik and others."
"959","940 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity on green vegetables. This hadith was narrated by a group from Musa ibn Talhah without connection; we do not know anyone who said in it 'from Musa, from his father' except al-Harith ibn Nabhan from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, nor do we know Ata narrated from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, except this hadith."
"960","941 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father."
"961","942 - Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated it to us, he said: My uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you — so how do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim; and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim — indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. This hadith was narrated by others besides al-Hakam ibn Marwan from Isra'il, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, without saying 'from his father'; Sharik concurred in connecting it."
"962","943 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah and Isa ibn Talhah, from their father, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a bedouin: Ask him about {those who fulfilled their vow} — who is he — while these did not dare ask him. The bedouin asked him: Who fulfilled his vow? He turned away from him, then he asked him and he turned away, then he exited through the mosque door with me beside him, and said: Where is the asker about who fulfilled his vow? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is of those who fulfilled their vow. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah through a connected route except through this route with this chain."
"963","944 - A man of the people of hadith — Amr ibn Malik — narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Talhah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Amr ibn al-As is indeed sound in judgment. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah except through this route with this chain."
"964","945 - Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan al-Bajali narrated to us — I think — from al-Hakam, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took in advance from al-Abbas the charity of two years. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated except al-Hasan al-Bajali — he is al-Hasan ibn Umarah — and al-Hasan: the people of knowledge have remained silent about his hadith."
"965","Among what Yahya ibn Talhah narrated from his father Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 946 - Imran ibn Harun al-Basri narrated to us — he was a veiled shaykh with only this hadith, residing near al-Khuraybah, whom people frequented to hear this hadith from him — he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with us at Makkah while fasting, and fasting wearied him; so we milked a she-camel of ours into a large cup and poured honey over it, honouring the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it at his breaking fast. When the sun set we handed him the cup; when he tasted it he gestured with his hand as if saying: What is this? We said: Milk and honey with which we wished to honour you — I think he said: May Allah honour you as you honoured me — or a supplication to this effect. Then he said: Whoever is moderate, Allah enriches him; whoever squanders, Allah impoverishes him; whoever is humble, Allah raises him; whoever is arrogant, Allah shatters him. Abu Bakr said: They used to write it from him before we were born. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain; we heard it only from Imran ibn Harun."
"966","Remainder of what Yahya ibn Talhah narrated from his father. 947 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw the crescent would say: O Allah, let it rise upon us with security, faith, safety, peace and Islam — my Lord and your Lord is Allah. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah except through this route with this chain."
"967","948 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Isa and Yahya, the two sons of Talhah, from their father Talhah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face. He said: A camel branded on its face was led past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If only this fire were kept away from this animal's face. I said: I shall brand in the farthest place — so I branded at the root of the tail. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah except through this route with this chain."
"968","949 - Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from his father, from his grandfather Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a quince in his hand, and he said: Take it, O Abu Muhammad, for it comforts the heart. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah except with this chain."
"969","950 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the meaning of 'Subhan Allah,' and he said: Declaring Allah, blessed and exalted, free of evil. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah connected except through this route with this chain."
"970","Among what Isa ibn Talhah narrated from his father Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 951 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Isa ibn Talhah, from his father, that two men were brethren; the one superior in Talhah's view died, and the other remained after him such-and-such, fasted Ramadan and prayed such-and-such, then died. Talhah saw in a dream that the latter in death was superior to the former and higher in rank. Talhah said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Did he not remain after him living such-and-such, fasting such? I said: Yes. He said: Between them is farther than between heaven and earth. This hadith has been narrated from Talhah through other routes; Isa narrated from his father another hadith in which Yahya shared with him, about branding on the face, which we mentioned in Yahya ibn Talhah's hadith."
"971","Among what Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated from his father Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 952 - Ali ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Uthman, narrated to us, from his father, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, he said: A group of polytheists were around the Ka'bah, among them Abu Jahl, may Allah curse him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, stood over them and said: Evil faces. They fell silent — none uttered a word. I looked at Abu Jahl excusing himself to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Hold back from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall not hold back from you — or: I shall kill you. Abu Jahl said: Can you do that? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will kill you. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah except through this route with this chain."
"972","Among what Aslam, freedman of Umar, narrated from Talhah. 953 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubadah al-Ansari — he is al-Zuraqi — narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from his father, he said: I witnessed Uthman ibn Affan on the day he was besieged, with people in the funeral place — had a pebble been cast it would fall only upon a man's head. I saw Uthman look over them from the skylight facing the Maqam — the station of Jibril, peace be upon him — and say: Is Talhah among you? They were silent. He said: Is Talhah among you? They were silent. He said: Is Talhah among you? Uthman said: I never thought a group hearing my call three times would not answer me. I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah — do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at such-and-such place, with none but you and me with him, and said: O Talhah, every prophet has a companion of his ummah in Paradise, and this Uthman is my companion in Paradise? He said: O Allah, yes — and he left. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Uthman ibn Affan nor from Talhah, may Allah have mercy on them, except through this route with this chain."
"973","Among what Abdullah ibn Shaddad narrated from Talhah. 954 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim, a freedman of ours, narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Talhah, that three men of the Udhrah tribe came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he sent to one of his wives but they had nothing to suffice them. He said: Who will suffice them? Talhah said: I will suffice them for you — so I sufficed them. Talhah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition and one of them went out and was killed; then he sent another expedition and the second went out and was killed; then the third fell ill, wasted away upon his bed and died. Talhah saw them in sleep — the first to enter Paradise was the one who died upon his bed, then the second, then the third. He mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do you not know that he prayed — or said: with his prayer, fasting, glorification and such-and-such. We do not know Abdullah ibn Shaddad narrated from Talhah except this hadith."
"974","Among what Rabi'ah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hudayr narrated from Talhah. 955 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ma'n narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Rabi'ah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hudayr, he said: I accompanied Talhah ibn Ubaydullah and never heard him narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) aught except that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the graves of the martyrs; when we descended from Harrah Waqim we saw graves at the mountain's bend and said: O Messenger of Allah, these are our brethren. He said: These are our companions. Then we went out until we came to the martyrs' graves, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the graves of our brethren — and he supplicated for them. These words we do not know to be narrated except from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah with this chain."
"975","Among what Salim al-Makki narrated from his father, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. 956 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salim al-Makki, from his father, he said: I came to Madinah with a milch animal of mine and met Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, mentioning that to him. He said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman selling for a bedouin, I would sell for you — but bargain, and consult me and I shall advise you."
"976","957 - Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salim al-Makki, from a man, from Talhah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Talhah except through this route; we do not know anyone who said 'from Salim, from his father, from Talhah' except Mu'ammal from Hammad — others narrate it from a man."
"977","Among what Abu Iyas narrated from Talhah. 958 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Rifa'ah ibn Iyas narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah have mercy on him, say to Talhah on the day of al-Jamal: I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah — did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him? He said: Yes — then he recalled it and left. These words we do not know to be narrated from Talhah except with this chain; this Rifa'ah ibn Iyas we do not know anyone narrated from except al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan."
"978","Among what Abir al-Himyari narrated from Talhah. 959 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd al-Himyari, from his father, he said: I was with Uthman, may Allah have mercy on him, when he was besieged, and he said: Is Talhah here? Talhah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah — do you not know that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: Let each man of you take his companion's hand? You took the hand of so-and-so, so-and-so took so-and-so's hand, until each man took his companion's hand; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: This is my companion in this world and my ally in the Hereafter. He said: O Allah, yes. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from Uthman nor from Talhah except through this route with this chain. Some of what was narrated from Talhah is unconnected from Talhah, and some has been entered into the Musnad."
"979","960 - Of that is what Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays — and Abu Usamah from Isma'il, from Qays, he said: I saw Talhah's hand with which he shielded the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — it had become paralyzed."
"980","961 - Of it is what Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated. He said: Talhah used to say: Shall I not tell you aught I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Amr ibn al-As is of the righteous of Quraysh; and what an excellent household: Abdullah, Abu Abdullah and Umm Abdullah. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"981","Musnad al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him). Beginning of al-Zubayr's Musnad. Among what Abdullah ibn Umar narrated from al-Zubayr. 962 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather Hayyan ibn Bistam, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when he passed by Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr while he was crucified, and said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Khubayb — I heard your father, meaning al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it in this world and the Hereafter. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from al-Zubayr except through this route with this chain, nor do we know Ibn Umar narrated from al-Zubayr except this hadith."
"982","Among what Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from his father al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. 963 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: al-Zubayr said: When was revealed {Then you shall surely be asked that Day about bliss}, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss shall we be asked about — when they are but the two black things: dates and water? He said: That shall indeed be. This hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from al-Zubayr with this chain."
"983","964 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Indeed you will die, and indeed they will die; then on the Day of Resurrection you will dispute before your Lord}, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, will what passed between us in this world be repeated upon us, along with minor sins? He said: Yes — it shall indeed be repeated upon you until every holder of a right is given his right. Al-Zubayr said: The matter is indeed grave."
"984","965 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned something similar. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"985","966 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I was in the fortress on the day of al-Khandaq, I and Umar ibn Abi Salamah — he would stoop for me so I could watch the fighting, and I would stoop for him so he could watch. I saw my father that day coming and going, charging these then charging those. When he returned I said: O father, I saw you today coming and going, charging these once and those once. He said: Did you see me, my son? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me both his parents. This hadith has been narrated from al-Zubayr through other routes; this chain is among the finest chains narrated on that."
"986","967 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dinar informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One or two sucks do not prohibit, nor one or two sips. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr through other routes; we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, except Muhammad ibn Dinar from Hisham."
"987","968 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on a cold night — or a cold morning — so I went, then came back with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with one of his wives under a blanket, and he cast upon me the edge of a garment. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated except al-Zubayr, nor do we know for it a chain other than this chain; we do not know anyone corroborated Ishaq ibn Idris in this narration."
"988","969 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that a man of the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam over the streams of al-Harrah with which they watered the palms. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then release the water to your neighbour. The Ansari became angry and said: You judged for him because he is your aunt's son? The Messenger of Allah's face changed colour, then said: O Zubayr, irrigate, then withhold the water until it reaches the embankment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took al-Zubayr's full right. Al-Zubayr said: I think the verse was revealed about that: {But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what disputes arise between them}. This hadith was narrated by Yunus ibn Yazid from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I disputed with a man of the Ansar over the streams of al-Harrah — then he mentioned something similar. We do not know these words narrated except from al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"989","970 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I said to my father: O father, why do I not hear you narrate from the Messenger of Allah as so-and-so and so-and-so narrate? He said: Though I never parted him since I embraced Islam, I heard him say: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"990","971 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Bayan narrated to us, from Wabarah, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I said to al-Zubayr: Why do I not hear you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as his companions — so-and-so, so-and-so and so-and-so — narrate from him? He said: Though I never part him since I embraced Islam, I heard him say: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Bayan except Khalid ibn Abdullah, nor from Jami' ibn Shaddad except Shu'bah. It was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ali ibn Abi Talib, though their chains were not strong — so we mentioned it from al-Zubayr as it had the soundest chain. It is narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Abdullah ibn Abbas, Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Amr; some forty men narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"991","972 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail on the day of Uhud; he rose toward the rock but could not, so Talhah sat beneath him until he stood upon the rock. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Talhah has earned it. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from al-Zubayr except through this route."
"992","973 - Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I was of those overcome by drowsiness on the day of Uhud — I shall never forget hearing the voice of Mu'attib ibn Qushayr as in a dream."
"993","Among what Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan narrated from al-Zubayr. 974 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to al-Zubayr: I adjure you by Allah, by whose permission heaven and earth stand — did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity? He said: O Allah, yes."
"994","975 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, that Umar ibn al-Khattab adjured al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam among a group: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity? They said: Yes. We do not know Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan narrated from al-Zubayr except this hadith."
"995","Among what Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated from al-Zubayr. 976 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Sabiri narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Shaddad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Mutarrif, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, concerning Allah's words: {And fear a trial which will not afflict only those of you who wronged}, he said: We would converse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, never thinking we were its people — until it befell us. We do not know Mutarrif narrated from al-Zubayr except this hadith."
"996","Among what al-Bahiyy narrated from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. 977 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Wa'il ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-Bahiyy, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: None shall be killed here after this day by detention except a man who kills Uthman ibn Affan. This hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from al-Zubayr with this chain."
"997","Among what Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from his father al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. 978 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Umm Urwah bint Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from her father, from her grandfather al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud and placed his wives and his aunt Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib in a fortress called Fari' with Hassan ibn Thabit, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud. A Jew climbed until he looked over the Messenger's wives and his aunt. Safiyyah said: O Hassan, rise to him and kill him. He said: By Allah, that is not in me — had it been in me I would have gone out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Safiyyah said: Tie the sword upon my arm. He said: Then she advanced to him until she killed him and cut off his head, and said to him: Take the head and throw it at the Jews. He said: That is not in me. So she herself took the head and threw it at the Jews; the Jews said: We knew Muhammad would not leave his family behind with none among them — so they dispersed and left. Aishah said: Sa'd ibn Mu'adh passed, saying — she said — I never saw anyone more handsome than him that day; upon him was a trace of yellowness, and upon him a short coat of mail; he had married and consummated with his wife days before, so upon him was a trace of saffron. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) charged the disbelievers, Hassan would open the fortress, and when they countered he would retreat with them. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from al-Zubayr except through this route with this chain."
"998","979 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Wazi' narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) displayed a sword on the day of Uhud and said: Who will take this sword with its right? Abu Dujanah Simak ibn Kharashah stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall take it with its right — what is its right? He said: So he gave it to him and he went out; I followed him, and he would pass by naught but he split and tore it, until he came to women at the mountain's foot with Hind among them, saying: The cushions. He charged her, and she called: O family of Sakhr — none answered her, so he turned away. I said to him: All your deeds I saw and admired, except that you did not kill the woman. He said: She called and none answered her, so I disliked striking with the Messenger's sword a woman with no helper. This hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording connected except from al-Zubayr with this chain; we do not know anyone narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, except Ubaydullah ibn al-Wazi'."
"999","980 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, keeper of al-Sabiri, narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, he said: On the day of Uhud a woman came hurrying until she almost overlooked the slain; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked her seeing them and said: The woman, the woman. Al-Zubayr said: I looked at her — she was my mother Safiyyah. We went out hurrying to her, and I said: Go back — I reached her before she reached the slain. She struck my chest and said: Away from me — may you have no mother. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return — or halt. So she halted and produced two garments she had brought, saying: These two garments I brought for my brother Hamzah, for his killing has reached me — shroud him in them. He said: We came to Hamzah to shroud him in them, but beside him was a man of the Ansar with whom was done what was done to Hamzah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked shrouding Hamzah in two garments while the Ansari had no shroud. So we said: For Hamzah a garment and for the Ansari a garment; we measured them — one was larger than the other — so we cast lots between them and shrouded each in the garment that fell to him. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"1000","981 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: al-Zubayr said: Concerning us was revealed this verse: {Blood relatives are more entitled to one another in Allah's Book}. That is because we came to Madinah and took the Ansar as brethren — Abu Bakr had taken Kharijah ibn Zayd as brother, and Umar had taken Itban ibn Malik as brother. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, except Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"1001","982 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to take his rope, go and bring a bundle of firewood, sell it and shield his face with it — is better for him than asking people, whether they give him or withhold. This hadith we do not know to be narrated from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam except through this route."
"1002","983 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, he said: I was of those overcome by drowsiness on the day of Uhud."
"1003","984 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps one of you beats his wife as a slave is beaten — indeed the best of you are the best to their wives. This hadith: the account 'the best of you are the best to their wives' was narrated by more than one from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, unconnected; some of Hisham's companions connected it. As for the account of beating women, Hisham narrated it from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zam'ah — thus a group narrated it; al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated it from Hisham, from his father, from Aishah. We do not know anyone who narrated it from Hisham, from his father, from al-Zubayr, except Mughirah ibn Muslim; we heard it only from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, from Shababab, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim."
"1004","985 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shababab narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather al-Zubayr — thus Shababab narrated it from al-Mughirah, from Hisham, from his father, from al-Zubayr, in what Zakariyya narrated to us — that they slaughtered a horse in the Messenger's time (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate it. This hadith is narrated by Abu Usamah from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr, from Asma bint Abi Bakr."
"1005","986 - Salih ibn Mu'adh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, bless my religion which is the safeguard of my affair, my Hereafter to which is my destination, and my worldly life wherein is my sustenance; make my life an increase in every good, and make death a rest from every evil."
"1006","987 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning excursion in Allah's path and an evening one are better than the world and what is in it."
"1007","988 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I gathered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Madinah on the day of Uhud — none of the Messenger's Companions remained — meaning at Madinah — until many of the Messenger's Companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were slain. A crier cried: Muhammad has been killed. Women wept, and a woman said: Do not hasten to weep until I see. She went out walking with no concern but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asking about him. End of the tenth part — the end of al-Zubayr's hadith."
"1008","Musnad Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him). Beginning of the eleventh part — first of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf's Musnad. Ibn Abbas from him. 989 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ibn Abbas."
"1009","990 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas — the wording is Malik's — that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to Sham until at Sargh he was met by the commanders of the armies, among them Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and his companions, who told him the plague had fallen upon Sham. Ibn Abbas said: Umar said: Call the Muhajirun for me — so they called them and he consulted them, telling them the plague had fallen upon Sham. Some said: You went out for an affair; we see no reason for you to turn back. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; when it falls in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it. So Umar praised Allah and turned back. This hadith has been narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf through other routes; these two hadiths we mentioned are the highest narrated on that from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and the sounder of the two chains is Malik ibn Anas from al-Zuhri. Sa'd ibn Malik, Usamah ibn Zayd and others narrated it."
"1010","991 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf — thus Ibn Abi Hafsah said: from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I am al-Rahman and it is the womb (rahim) — I derived for it from My name; whoever joins it I join him, and whoever severs it I cut him off. This hadith was narrated by Ibn Uyaynah."
"1011","992 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visited Abu al-Raddad and said: I know none more dutiful and joining than Abu Muhammad? Abd al-Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I am al-Rahman and it is the womb — I derived for it from My name; whoever joins it I join him, and whoever severs it I cut him off. Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father. The correct is what Ibn Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah. These words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other routes — Abu Hurayrah, Aishah and Abdullah ibn Amr narrated it with similar words."
"1012","993 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Raddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1013","994 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Husayn, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to me, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf."
"1014","995 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you prays and doubts whether one or two, let him count it one; when he doubts whether two or three, let him count it two, until the doubt is in the addition — then let him prostrate two prostrations, then greet. Thus al-Muharibi and Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, without inserting anyone between Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Makhul — from Ibrahim's narration."
"1015","996 - According to what Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us. He said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. The one who inserted a man between Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Makhul came in his narration with the like of Ibrahim ibn Sa'd's narration, adding a man whom Ibrahim dropped; sufficient for you is the preservation and precision of Isma'il ibn Ibrahim."
"1016","997 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When you are in doubt about a deficiency, pray until you are in doubt about an excess."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, except Ismail ibn Muslim; and this Ismail ibn Muslim is not strong in hadith, though al-A'mash and others narrated from him."
"1017","998 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Thawr, meaning Ibn Zayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew us up in ranks on the night of Badr for the day of Badr."
"1018","999 - Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn, from Makhul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1019","Among what Jubayr ibn Mut'im narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1000 - Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I witnessed the alliance of al-Mutayyabin while I was a boy with my uncles, and I would not like to break it, nor that I had broken it, even for red camels."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, and it has been narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf through more than one channel; and this chain is the best chain narrated on that from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. And Jubayr narrated from Abdur-Rahman nothing but this hadith."
"1020","Jabir ibn Abdillah from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1001 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and set out to the palm trees, and found therein Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him and placed him in his lap, and his eyes shed tears. Then he said: ""O my little son, I own nothing for you against Allah."" So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you weep - did you not forbid weeping? He said: ""I only forbade wailing: two foolish wicked voices - a voice at a blessing with play and amusement and the flutes of Satan, and a voice at a calamity with scratching of faces and tearing of garments and the jingle of Satan. He who does not show mercy is not shown mercy. Were it not that it is truth and a true promise, and that both are a path that must come and cannot be avoided until the last of us joins the first of us, we would have grieved a grief severer than this"" - meaning for him - ""and indeed we are grieved for him. The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say what angers the Lord, Mighty and Majestic."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman except through this channel with this chain. And part of these words has been narrated from Abdur-Rahman with another chain."
"1021","1002 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, from Amir al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl: ""Who struck your father?"" So Ikrimah said: The one who cut off my father's leg. So he awarded his spoils to Mu'adh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh. These words, we do not know anyone who narrated them with this wording, connected, except Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf; and this Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah is weak in hadith, and as for Amir al-Ansari - Ishaq ibn Abdillah did not give his lineage."
"1022","Among what Anas ibn Malik narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1003 - Ismail ibn Ibrahim, the companion of al-Quhi, narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Shu'bah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that he married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold; so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw on me the cheerfulness of a wedding. I said: I have married a woman of the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone of gold."
"1023","1004 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it, except that he said: ""Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf ... and these two said: from Anas, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf."
"1024","Among what Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father. 1005 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Abdur-Rahman, you are among the rich, and you will not enter Paradise except crawling; so lend to Allah and He will free your feet."" So Abdur-Rahman said: What shall I lend or give out? And Abdur-Rahman went out; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him and said: ""Command Abdur-Rahman to host the guest, feed the poor, and give the beggar, for that will suffice him for much of what he is in."" We do not know Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, except this hadith."
"1025","Chapter of what Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated from his father, from his grandfather Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1006 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: Five or four of his Companions would never leave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day he came out and I followed him; he entered a garden of the gardens of al-Aswaf, and prayed, and prostrated, prolonging the prostration. So I said: Allah has taken the soul of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I shall never see him again. So I grieved and wept. He raised his head and saw me, and called me, and said: ""What is the matter with you, or what has alarmed you?"" So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the prostration, so I said: Allah has taken His Messenger; I shall never see him again - so I grieved and wept. He said: ""I prostrated this prostration in gratitude to my Lord for what He has bestowed upon me regarding my Ummah. Then he said: Whoever of them sends blessings upon you, ten good deeds are written for him."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim except Qays ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, nor did anyone narrate it from Qays except Musa ibn Ubaydah; and it has been narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf through another, disconnected channel."
"1026","1007 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: My name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abdur-Rahman. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. And we do not know for it a chain from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except this chain."
"1027","1008 - Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Salih ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, that he said: I hunted a bird with a qunbulah (snare); my father Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf caught up with me and said: O my son, from where did you take it? I said: From al-Qunbulah, a place in Madinah. So he rubbed my ear, then took it and released it. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hunting game between its two lava tracts. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain."
"1028","1009 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that food was brought to him - Shu'bah said: I think he was fasting - and he said: Hamzah was killed and we found nothing with which to shroud him, though he was better than me; and Mus'ab ibn Umayr was killed, though he was better than me, and we found nothing with which to shroud him; and we have attained of it (the world) what we have attained. Abdur-Rahman said: ""I fear that our good deeds have been hastened for us in this world."" Sa'd said: ""And I think he did not eat, may Allah have mercy on him."" This hadith we include in the Musnad because it was related about Hamzah and Mus'ab, and both were struck on the day of Uhud."
"1029","1010 - Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur and Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Bazzar narrated to us, from dictation, they said: Muhammad ibn al-A'la al-Madini narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman except through this channel with this chain."
"1030","1011 - Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-A'la narrated to us, he said: While I was with al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he found two fallen dates; he took one and gave me the other, but I refused to eat it. Then he said to me: My father informed me, from my grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate it - meaning a date. These words, we do not know them narrated except from Abdur-Rahman with this chain."
"1031","1012 - Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-A'la narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: A daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him that her daughter was overpowered (dying); so he said to the messenger: ""Say to her: To Allah belongs what He takes, and to Allah belongs what He leaves."" Then she sent to him a second time, and he returned to her the like of that. Then she sent to him a third time, so he came to her with some of his Companions; the little girl was brought out to him while her soul was rattling in her chest. So he felt pity for her and his eyes shed tears; one of his Companions noticed him while they were looking at him when his eyes shed tears, and he said: ""What is the matter with you that you look? It is a mercy which Allah places where He wills; Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain."
"1032","1013 - Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi and Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, they said: Yusuf ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Abdur-Rahman, he said: While I was standing in the rank on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and to my left, and there I was between two boys of the Ansar whose teeth were young (of tender age); so I wished I were between two stronger than them. One of them said to me: O uncle, do you know Abu Jahl? I said: Yes; what need have you of him, O son of my brother? He said: I have been told that he reviles the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or: insults the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I see him, my person shall not part from his person until the more helpless of us dies. So I marvelled at that; then the other nudged me and said the like of it, so I marvelled at their words. No sooner had I looked at Abu Jahl moving - or: shifting - among the people than I said to them: Lo, this is your man about whom you ask me. So they rushed at him with their two swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. He said: ""Which of you killed him?"" Each one of them said: I killed him. He said: ""Did you wipe your swords?"" They said: No. So he looked at the two swords and said: ""Both of you killed him."" And he awarded his spoils to Mu'adh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh; and they were Mu'adh ibn Afra and Mu'adh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh, the two who struck Abu Jahl. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel with this chain; and Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn is a well-known, trustworthy man."
"1033","1014 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was leading the people in prayer; he wanted to step back, so he gestured to him: (stay in) your place. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed following the prayer of Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf."
"1034","1015 - Ali ibn al-Fadl al-Karabisi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: Umayyah ibn Khalaf said to me."
"1035","1016 - And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Umayyah ibn Khalaf said to me: O Abd al-Ilah, who is the man marked with an ostrich feather on his chest on the day of Badr? I said: That is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); that is Hamzah ibn Abdil-Muttalib. He said: He is the one who did to us the deeds (of havoc). This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman except through this channel; it enters into the Musnad because he related of the deed of Hamzah and his fighting on the day of Badr."
"1036","1017 - Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Sa'd ibn Mu'adh came; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is your chief."" This hadith has been narrated by other than Iyad ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father; and we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain."
"1037","1018 - Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Quraysh, and the Ansar, and Juhaynah, and Muzaynah, and Aslam, and Ghifar, and Ashja' are allies; they have no protector besides Allah and His Messenger."" This hadith has been narrated by Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah; and this hadith of Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from his grandfather - Amr ibn Yahya has not been corroborated in it, from his father, from Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, with this narration."
"1038","Among what Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated from his father. 1019 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, he said: ""I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... and I was among the first people to accept Islam."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz; and we heard it only from Abdullah ibn Shabib."
"1039","1020 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad Abu ar-Rabi' al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abdur-Rahman, and Sa'id ibn Zayd, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah's mercy be upon them."""
"1040","1021 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ad-Darawardi narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Humayd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. And he did not say: from his grandfather. This hadith mentions in it Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, making him the tenth; and we do not know it narrated except from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, though more than one has narrated it mursal."
"1041","1022 - And Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, from Humayd ibn al-Qasim ibn Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: When death came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: O Messenger of Allah, counsel us. He said: ""I counsel you regarding the first forerunners, and their sons after them, and their sons after them, and their sons after them; if you do not do so, neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from you."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf with this chain; and we heard the hadith of Ja'far ibn Awn only from Bishr ibn Khalid."
"1042","1023 - Zurayq ibn as-Sakht narrated to us, he said: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan al-Bajali narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: A short spear would be brought out for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the two Eids, until he would pray towards it; and he would say thirteen takbirs. And Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah's mercy and pleasure be upon them, would do that. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain; and this al-Hasan al-Bajali is lenient in hadith, and people have remained silent about his hadith; and I think he is al-Hasan ibn Umarah."
"1043","1024 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ad-Darawardi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Musa, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather Abdur-Rahman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I witnessed the alliance of Banu Hashim, and Zuhrah, and Taym; it would not please me to have broken it even for red camels; and if I were called to it today I would answer, upon enjoining right, and forbidding wrong, and taking for the oppressed from the oppressor."" This hadith has been narrated from Abdur-Rahman about the story of the alliance with other than this wording."
"1044","Among what Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated from his father. 1025 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Isa al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One who fasts Ramadan while travelling is like one who breaks fast while resident."" This hadith, Usamah ibn Zayd raised it (as marfu'), and Yunus corroborated him in its chain. And Ibn Abi Dhi'b and others narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, as mawquf, from the words of Abdur-Rahman. And even if it were established as marfu', the going out of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went out and fasted until he reached al-Kadid, then broke fast, and commanded us to break fast, would be a proof of the abrogation of this hadith if it were established; for one takes the later and later of the deed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1045","1026 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Yamin narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: Qasamah regarding blood took place on the day of Khaybar; that was because a man of the Ansar, of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was lost under the night; so the Ansar came and said: Our companion is weltering in his blood. He said: ""Do you know his killer?"" They said: No; indeed his killers are the Jews. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Choose from them fifty men, and let them swear by Allah with the strongest of their oaths; then take the blood-money from them."" So they did. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain, and we heard it only from Abu Kurayb; and this Abdur-Rahman ibn Yamin - Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated from him, as did Abd al-Hamid ibn Abdur-Rahman Abu Yahya al-Himmani."
"1046","1027 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Mus'ab, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The adornment of the world will be lifted in the year one hundred and twenty-five."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, and we do not know for it a path except this path."
"1047","1028 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Mus'ab, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of you are the best of you to their families, and I am the best of you to my family."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman except through this channel with this chain."
"1048","1029 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Afif ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father."
"1049","1030 - And Abdah ibn Abdillah narrated it to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah, meaning Ibn Shurayh, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan, may Allah curse him, said: The son of Adam will never escape me in one of three: taking wealth from other than its lawful (source), and placing it in other than its right, or withholding it from its right."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr said: He is not an Egyptian."
"1050","1031 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until two great parties fight, their claim being one."" This hadith has been narrated to us by other than Ibn Shabib, from Ibn Abi Uways, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1051","1032 - Muhammad ibn al-A'la al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Three things I swear upon: no wealth decreases from charity, so give charity; and no man pardons an injustice done to him except that Allah increases him in honour, so pardon and Allah will honour you; and no man opens upon himself a door of begging except that Allah opens upon him a door of poverty."" Thus Yunus ibn Khabbab narrated it, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father; and Umar ibn Abi Salamah differed with him in its chain."
"1052","1033 - So Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, he said: the storyteller of Palestine narrated to me, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, three things - and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I would indeed swear upon them: ""No wealth decreases from charity, so give charity; and no servant pardons an injustice seeking thereby the Face of Allah except that Allah raises him thereby a degree on the Day of Resurrection; and no man opens upon himself a door of begging except that Allah opens a door of poverty."" And the hadith of Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from the storyteller of Palestine, from Abdur-Rahman - is more correct than the hadith of Yunus ibn Khabbab."
"1053","1034 - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ibn Ulathah, and he is Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ulathah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The wicked oath removes wealth - or: takes away wealth."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel; and we do not know Hisham ibn Hassan narrating, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, other than this hadith; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hisham except Ibn Ulathah; and this Ibn Ulathah is lenient in hadith."
"1054","1035 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: ar-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beautify the Qur'an with your voices."" This hadith is narrated by al-Zuhri and Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah. And Salih ibn Musa, who narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Salamah, from his father, is lenient in hadith; and we mentioned this hadith only to make clear its defect. And this Salih ibn Musa narrated another hadith with this chain upon which he was not corroborated either."
"1055","1036 - Fudayl ibn Abdillah narrated it to us with it, he said: ar-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One who visits the sick is in the harvest-gathering (makhrafah) of Paradise; and when he sits with him, mercy covers him."" We have already mentioned this Salih ibn Musa, so we have no need to repeat mentioning him afterwards."
"1056","1037 - al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs al-Madini narrated to me, he said: al-Hasan ibn Uthman ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The briber and the bribed are in the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain. And Umar ibn Abi Salamah said in it: from his father, from Abu Hurayrah; and Ibn Abi Dhi'b said: from al-Harith ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"1057","1038 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: Islam came with dislike and hardship; so we found the best of good in dislike. So we went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah, and He made for us in that loftiness and triumph. And we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Badr upon the condition which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, mentioned: ""And indeed a party of the believers were averse - disputing with you about the truth after it had become clear, as though they were being driven to death while they looked on - and when Allah promised you one of the two parties, that it would be yours, and you wished that the one without thorns would be yours."" And the thorn was Quraysh. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made for us in that loftiness and triumph; so we found the best of good in dislike. These words, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf with this chain."
"1058","1039 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I had a promise with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so when Qurayzah was conquered, I came for him to fulfil for me what he had promised me; then I heard him saying: ""Whoever is self-sufficient, Allah will enrich him; and whoever is content, Allah will make him content."" So I said to myself: No doubt I shall not ask him for anything - (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman through a better path than this path."
"1059","1040 - Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: my father Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to me, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Humayd ibn Abdillah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in: ""When the sky splits"" ten times. Thus Ibn Abi Layla narrated it, from Humayd ibn Abdillah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father. And ath-Thawri narrated it, from Humayd, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah."
"1060","1041 - Muhammad ibn al-A'la narrated to us, and he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), set out seeking a man of the Ansar, and called him; so the Ansari came out with his head dripping water. He said: ""What is the matter with you?"" He said: I feared I would detain you, so I poured water over myself, then came out. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did you ejaculate?"" He said: No. He said: ""Then when you do that, do not bathe; wash what touched the woman of you, and perform ablution, your ablution for prayer."" This hadith has been narrated by others than those we mentioned, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id; and this act is abrogated - abrogated by what was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When the two circumcised parts meet, bathing becomes obligatory."" And this Zayd ibn Sa'd - we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Yunus ibn Bukayr."
"1061","1042 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Muslim is in the protection of Allah from the day his mother bore him until he stands before Allah, Blessed and Exalted; so if he meets Allah with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, truthfully, or with truthful seeking of forgiveness, Allah writes for him freedom from the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf with this chain."
"1062","1043 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah at-Tawil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""None will be kind to you after me except the truthful, the patient."" Abdur-Rahman said: So I sold something I had named, of Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh, for forty thousand, and divided it among them - meaning among the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah have mercy on them. This hadith has been narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf through another channel; and we do not know it narrated through a channel, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, better than this channel."
"1063","1044 - Ishaq ibn al-Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an; do not eat by it, nor seek preference by it, nor turn away from it, nor go to excess in it."" This hadith is a mistake; its mistake is only from Hammad ibn Yahya, because he is lenient in hadith. And the correct hadith is only narrated by Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Shibl."
"1064","1045 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abu Najih - or: Ibn Abi Najih - from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would say in the prayer over the dead: ""O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, and our present and our absent, and our male and our female, and our young and our old. Whomsoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam; and whomsoever of us You cause to die, cause him to die upon faith."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Salamah, from Abdur-Rahman, except through this channel; and Abu Hamzah ath-Thumali narrated it from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to that."
"1065","1046 - Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from some of the people of Makkah - they think he is Ibn Abi Najih - from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he finished his food he would say: ""Praise be to Allah Who fed us and gave us drink; praise be to Allah Who sufficed us and sheltered us; praise be to Allah Who bestowed favour upon us and preferred us. We ask You by Your mercy to protect us from the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, except through this channel with this chain."
"1066","1047 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zayd al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, he said: ""I was shown Paradise, and there it was: none enters it but the poor; so I entered with them crawling. Then when I woke up I said: my camels which I await in Syria, and their loads, are in the path of Allah, until I enter it with them walking."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Muhammad ibn Talhah."
"1067","1048 - Umar ibn Musa as-Sami narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman: narrate to me a hadith you heard from your father, which your father heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has made obligatory upon you the fasting of Ramadan, and I have established its standing (in prayer); so whoever fasts it with faith and seeking reward, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain, from the hadith of an-Nadr ibn Shayban; and more than one narrated it from an-Nadr."
"1068","1049 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Uthman ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his grandfather, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about beasts (lice/insects), so he commanded him to wear silk. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from his father, except through this channel with this chain."
"1069","Among what Mus'ab ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated from his father. 1050 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Jabr narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdillah ibn Hantab, from Mus'ab ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, he turned to at-Ta'if and besieged it seventeen or nineteen (days); then he stood as a speaker, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""I counsel you well regarding my kin; and your appointment is the Hawd (Pool). By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall establish prayer, and you shall give zakat, or I shall send to you a man from me, or like myself, who will strike your necks."" Then he took the hand of Ali and said: ""This one."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain; and we do not know Mus'ab narrating from his father except this hadith."
"1070","Among what Sahl ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated from his father Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1051 - One of our companions narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to us, from Abd al-Majid ibn Sahl ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says in a day, when he enters morning and when he enters evening: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is Living and does not die; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Powerful - his sins are forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain; and we do not know Sahl ibn Abdur-Rahman narrating from his father except this hadith."
"1071","And what Kathir ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated from his father Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1052 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Abdillah al-Bakri - or: an-Nukri - narrated to us, he said: a son of Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The womb calls out on the Day of Resurrection: whoever joins me, Allah joins him; and whoever cuts me, Allah cuts him."" And we do not know this son of Abdur-Rahman narrating from his father except this hadith."
"1072","Among what the shaykhs narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1053 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Muwarri' al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A protective invocation with which Ibrahim would protect Ishaq and Ismail, peace be upon them; and I protect with it al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them: Allah hears one who calls, for whoever calls - beyond Allah is a resort for whoever aims."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain."
"1073","1054 - Umar ibn al-Khattab as-Sijistani narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Damdam ibn Zur'ah narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Malik ibn Yukhamir as-Saksaki, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hijrah is two traits: that you abandon evil deeds, one of them; and the other that you emigrate to Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And hijrah does not cease as long as repentance is accepted; and repentance keeps being accepted until the sun rises from the west. Then when it rises, every heart is sealed with what is in it, and deeds suffice people."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman except through this channel."
"1074","1055 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, he said: a man of the people of at-Ta'if narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Shurahbil, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer, for it is in the Book of Allah al-Isha; the Bedouins only named it al-Atamah because of their camels, for their milking."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain."
"1075","1056 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Umar said: How do you deal with the Magians? So Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Apply to them the Sunnah of the People of the Book."" This hadith has been narrated by a group from Ja'far, from his father, and they did not say: from his grandfather; and his grandfather is Ali ibn al-Husayn. And the hadith is mursal; and we do not know anyone who said: from Ja'far, from his father, from his grandfather, except Abu Ali al-Hanafi, from Malik."
"1076","1057 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdillah ad-Dashtaki narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""How did you do regarding touching the two Corners?"" He said: I said: I did all of that - I touched and I left off. So he said: ""You did right."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except through this channel with this chain; and a group narrated it and did not say: from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf."
"1077","1058 - And ath-Thawri narrated it, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf - except that Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated it to us with it, and he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1078","1059 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his brother al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The thief does not guarantee his theft after the hadd is established."" This hadith is mursal, from Abdur-Rahman, because al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim did not meet Abdur-Rahman."
"1079","1060 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar: he heard Bajalah ibn Abd - and he is Bajalah ibn Abdah - he said: I was a scribe for Jaz' ibn Mu'awiyah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, when the letter of Umar came to us a month before his death: ""Kill every sorcerer, male and female; and separate every closely-related (couple) of the Magians; and forbid them wailing."" So we killed on one day three sorceresses; and we separated every man of the Magians from his unlawful (kinswoman) in the Book of Allah. And he prepared much food and invited them, and laid the sword upon his thigh; so they ate and did not wail. And they cast a camel-load or two camel-loads of silver. And Umar had not taken jizyah from the Magians until Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain."
"1080","1061 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Ibn Iyas al-Hudhali, he said: I heard Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the world, and neither he nor his family had eaten their fill of barley bread. End of the eleventh part."
"1081","Musnad of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him. Beginning of the twelfth part. Beginning of the Musnad of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. 1062 - Abu Abdillah informed us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Basri, known as al-Bazzar, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd in everything, until they said he does not pray well. He said: So Umar sent to him and said: They have complained about you in everything, until they claimed you do not pray well. So Sa'd said: By Allah, I would pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I would not fall short of it. I would pray the two Isha prayers, prolonging in the first two rak'ahs and shortening in the last two. He said: That is the opinion of you, O Abu Ishaq. So he sent with him a man or two men to ask the people of Kufah about him. When he came to them, he left no mosque but asked its people, and they mentioned good and said what is known (good), until he came to a mosque of Banu Abs. A man of them stood, nicknamed Abu Sa'dah, and said: Since you have adjured us, Sa'd would not march with the detachment, nor be just in judgment, nor divide equally. So Sa'd stood and said: By Allah, I shall surely supplicate against you with supplications: O Allah, if this servant of Yours is lying, prolong his life, intensify his poverty, and expose him to trials. Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said: So I saw him after that, an old man, advanced in age, afflicted with trial; when asked how he woke up, he would say: an old man, poor, afflicted with trial; the supplication of Sa'd has befallen me. Sa'd said: So I saw him, and he would expose himself to slave-girls in the roads, winking at them, while his eyebrows had fallen over his eyes from old age. This hadith, we do not know it narrated with these words except from Sa'd; and we do not know Jabir ibn Samurah narrating from Sa'd other than this hadith. And Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr and Abu Awn narrated it from Jabir ibn Samurah."
"1082","1063 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us with it, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abd al-Malik and Abu Awn, from Jabir ibn Samurah, similar to the hadith of Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik."
"1083","1064 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad, son of the brother of Waki', narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, similar to the hadith of Abu Awanah."
"1084","Among what Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated from Sa'id ibn Malik: what Ibn al-Munkadir narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd. 1065 - Muhammad ibn Abdil-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd - Sa'id said: then I met Sa'd, and he narrated to me - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."" We do not know Ibn al-Munkadir narrating from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, except this hadith; nor did anyone narrate it from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Yusuf al-Majishun. And Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated it from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this is the most correct chain narrated from Sa'd."
"1085","1066 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, the companion of as-Sabiri, narrated it to us with it, he said: Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1086","Among what Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1067 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for him his two parents, saying: ""Shoot; may my father and mother be ransom for you."" This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through more than one channel; and we do not know it narrated from Sa'd with a chain better than this chain."
"1087","1068 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Abd as-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""You are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."""
"1088","Among what al-Zuhri narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Malik, and he is Ibn Abi Waqqas. 1069 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard an-Nu'man ibn Rashid narrating from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah indeed refused Uthman ibn Maz'un celibacy (at-tabattul); and had He permitted him celibacy, we would have castrated ourselves."
"1089","1070 - And Umar ibn Musa as-Sami narrated it to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed refused Uthman ibn Maz'un celibacy; and had He given him permission, we would have castrated ourselves. He said: And we do not know these words narrated from Sa'd except from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Sa'd."
"1090","1071 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Dhuwayb ibn Imamah narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd."
"1091","1072 - And it was narrated to us another time from Usamah ibn Hafs, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love."" So he called Ali and gave him the banner. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Sa'd, except through this channel."
"1092","Ali ibn Zayd from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1073 - Abu al-Mutarrif Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz and Muhammad ibn Uqbah as-Sadusi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who am I? He said: ""You are Sa'd ibn Malik ibn Wuhayb ibn Abd Manaf; whoever says other than this, upon him is the curse of Allah."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Sa'd; and we do not know for it a chain from Sa'd other than this chain; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ali ibn Zayd except Ibn Uyaynah."
"1093","1074 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."""
"1094","1075 - And Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"1095","Among what Qatadah narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1076 - Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman ad-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."" This hadith was narrated from Qatadah by Ma'mar and Harb ibn Shaddad; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Harb except Ja'far ibn Sulayman. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dawud, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so I disapproved of it from him; and it is not known from the hadith of Ibn Abi Arubah, raised (marfu'), connected."
"1096","Among what Abu Suhayl ibn Malik narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1077 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah at-Tawil at-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhayl ibn Malik narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at al-Abbas and said: ""This is the uncle of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the most generous of Quraysh in hand, and the most affectionate towards them."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Sa'd with this chain. And this Muhammad ibn Talhah at-Taymi is a well-known man of the people of Madinah."
"1097","1078 - Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abu Suhayl ibn Malik, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were playing upon his belly. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you love them? So he said: ""Why should I not love them - my two sweet basils."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abbad ibn Ya'qub, from Ali ibn Hashim; and we do not know Abu Suhayl ibn Malik narrating from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, except these two hadiths."
"1098","Among what Hashim ibn Hashim narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1079 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: No one accepted Islam on the day I accepted Islam - meaning: not one - and I remained seven nights, a third of Islam. This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through more than this channel; and this chain is the best chain narrated on that. And this Hashim ibn Hashim - there is no harm in him; and more than one narrated from him."
"1099","1080 - Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Malij al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emptied for me his quiver - or: poured out for me the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his quiver - on the day of Uhud, and said: ""Shoot; may my father and mother be ransom for you."" This hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Marwan, from Hashim ibn Hashim."
"1100","Among what Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Labibah narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1081 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Labibah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: We would rent land for (a share of what grows on) water-channels and field-ridges, and for what the spring-water irrigates. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that, and commanded us to rent it for gold or silver. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and this Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Labibah is a man of the people of Madinah; Ibrahim ibn Sa'd and others narrated from him."
"1101","Among what al-Hadrami narrated from Sa'id, from Sa'd. 1082 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Hadrami - and he is called: al-Hadrami ibn Ishaq, and it is said: Ibn Lahiq - from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""There is no contagion, nor omen, nor hamah; and if there is omen, it is in the horse, and the woman, and the house."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated from this al-Hadrami except Yahya ibn Abi Kathir."
"1102","Among what Amir ibn Sa'd narrated from his father: among what Mujahid narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd. 1083 - Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, that he proposed to a woman in Makkah while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Would that I had with me one who saw her, or one who would inform me about her. So an effeminate man called Hit said: I shall describe her: when she comes forward, you say she walks with four; and when she turns away, you say she walks with eight. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do I not see that this one knows women."" And he would enter upon Sawdah, so he forbade her to let him enter upon her. Then when he came to Madinah, he banished him; and he remained thus until the rule of Umar. Then he exerted himself, and he would permit him to enter Madinah, so he would beg every Friday. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except his son Amir; nor did anyone narrate it from Amir ibn Sa'd except Mujahid; nor did anyone narrate it from Mujahid except Abd al-Karim; nor did anyone narrate it from Abd al-Karim except Ibn Abi Layla; nor did anyone narrate it from Ibn Abi Layla except Isa ibn al-Mukhtar; nor did anyone narrate it from Isa except Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman. And we do not know Mujahid narrating, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except this hadith."
"1103","Al-Zuhri from Amir. 1084 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The greatest of Muslims in crime against Muslims is one who asked about a matter that had not been forbidden, and it was forbidden because of his asking."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except his son Amir ibn Sa'd; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir except al-Zuhri; and none narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd."
"1104","1085 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: I fell ill in Makkah in the year of the Conquest; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me visiting me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and I have only one daughter; so shall I give in charity two-thirds of my wealth? He said: No. I said: Half? He said: No. I said: A third? He said: ""A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs rich, it is better for you than leaving them dependent, begging people. You will never spend an expenditure seeking thereby the Face of Allah except that you are rewarded in it, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind from my hijrah? He said: ""If you are left behind after me and do a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Last Abode, except that you are rewarded, or a degree is raised for you thereby. And perhaps if you are left behind, peoples will benefit by you and others will be harmed by you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their hijrah, and do not turn them back upon their heels. But the wretched Sa'd ibn Khawlah"" - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt pity for him that he died in Makkah. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. And others than al-Zuhri narrated it also. And it was narrated from A'ishah and from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Sa'd, regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deeming a third much."
"1105","1086 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the gecko and named it a little wicked one (fuwaysiq). This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from Amir, from him; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir ibn Sa'd except al-Zuhri; nor from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar; nor from Ma'mar except Abd ar-Razzaq - except a hadith in which Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah erred, and he is weak in hadith, so he narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, from Sa'd, and it is a mistake of Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah."
"1106","1087 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd ar-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he gave to men and did not give a man. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave so-and-so and so-and-so, and left so-and-so, you did not give him, though he is a believer? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. Then he said: ""I give to men and leave one who is more beloved to me than them, fearing they will be thrown into the Fire upon their faces."" These words were narrated from Sa'd, and from Amr ibn Taghlib, and from others than them; and the hadith of Sa'd is a sound chain, so we sufficed with it."
"1107","1088 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, and he said: A group came and asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he gave them and left a man. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave so-and-so and withheld from so-and-so, though he is a believer. He said: Or a Muslim. Then he said: ""I give the gift to a man, though another is more beloved to me than him, fearing Allah will throw him into the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except Amir; nor did anyone narrate it from Amir except al-Zuhri; and Ma'mar and Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated it from al-Zuhri."
"1108","1089 - Zayd ibn Akhzam and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my father? He said: In the Fire. He said: Then where is your father? He said: ""Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him tidings of the Fire."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Sa'd; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd except Yazid ibn Harun."
"1109","1090 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn ad-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah, son of the brother of al-Zuhri, from his uncle Ibn Shihab, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the voluntary (subhah) prayer upon his mount, wherever it turned with him; and he would not do that in the obligatory. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except al-Zuhri; nor did anyone narrate it from al-Zuhri except his nephew, from him. And others than the nephew of al-Zuhri narrate this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father."
"1110","Among what Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1091 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that Sa'd ibn Mu'adh judged regarding Banu Qurayzah that every one of them upon whom the razor has run (grown pubes) be killed, and that their offspring and wealth be divided. So that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""He has judged among them with the judgment of Allah with which He judged from above seven heavens."" This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one channel; and the highest who narrated that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Sa'd. And we do not know for it, from Sa'd, a path except this path - except a hadith narrated by Iyad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, and he was not corroborated in it."
"1111","1092 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: ""When the bier of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh passed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne has indeed shaken for him."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1112","Among what Salim Abu an-Nadr narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1093 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, he said: Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Salim Abu an-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd."
"1113","1094 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated it to us, he said: Abu Mushir narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Salim Abu an-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, he said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testifying for anyone that he is of the people of Paradise except for Abdullah ibn Salam. He said: ""There shall enter upon you a man of the people of Paradise."" So Abdullah ibn Salam entered. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Malik with this chain; and some of them added in it, he said: And this verse was revealed: ""And a witness from the Children of Israel testified to the like of it, and believed, while you were arrogant."" And we do not know anyone who narrated these words except Sa'd."
"1114","1095 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Salim Abu an-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This pain is a punishment, or a remainder of a punishment with which those before you were punished. So when it occurs in a land and you are not in it, do not go to it; and when it occurs in a land and you are in it, do not leave it."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from ath-Thawri, from Salim Abu an-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except Musa ibn Mas'ud. And others than Musa narrated it from ath-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir, from his father."
"1115","Among what Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. 1096 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This pain is a punishment and a torment with which those before you were tormented. So when it occurs in a land and you are in it, do not leave it; and when it occurs in a land and you are not in it, do not go to it."" These words, we mentioned them only from Sa'd because they differ in wording from what Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf narrated regarding plague. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Amir ibn Sa'd, from Usamah ibn Zayd. And this hadith, thus ath-Thawri and others narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father - except Abu Hudhayfah, for he narrated it from ath-Thawri, from Salim Abu an-Nadr."
"1116","1097 - Muhammad ibn as-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Of the happiness of the servant is his seeking good (istikharah) from his Lord, and his being pleased with what He decrees; and of the wretchedness of the servant is his abandoning istikharah, and his anger at what Allah decrees - or: after the decree."" This hadith was narrated by Amr ibn Ali from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd. And Imran said: from Abdur-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. And this Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr is lenient in hadith."
"1117","Among what Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj narrated from Amir, from his father. 1098 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ""that of which much intoxicates, (even) little of it."""
"1118","1099 - And Abdullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Kathir ibn Sinan narrated to us, from ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and a group narrated it from ad-Dahhak, raising it (musnad): among them ad-Darawardi and al-Walid ibn Kathir, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir al-Madini."
"1119","Among what Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from Amir. 1100 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ""would greet to his right, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen, and to his left, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen."" It has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he would greet to his right and to his left: from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and from Abdullah ibn Umar, and from Abdullah ibn Zayd, and from Wa'il ibn Hujr, and from Abu Humayd as-Sa'idi among ten of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Talq ibn Ali, and from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, and from Ammar ibn Yasir, and from Abu Rimthah, and from al-Bara and others. And this hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through more than one channel."
"1120","1101 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that when death came to him he said: ""Make a lahd for me, and set up bricks over me upright, as was done for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" This hadith, thus Abu Amir narrated it from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. And Ishaq ibn Muhammad said: from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather. And Abu Amir is more established than Ishaq ibn Muhammad. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1121","1102 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that he rode to his palace at al-Aqiq, and found a slave-boy cutting a tree, so he stripped him (of his clothes/goods). When Sa'd returned, the people of the slave came asking him to return to them what he had taken from their slave-boy. So he said: ""Allah forbid that I return anything the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me as spoils"" - and he refused to return it to them. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except Amir."
"1122","1103 - Muhammad ibn Isa at-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail, one over the other, on the day of Uhud. And Salm is higher than Sa'd. And we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1123","1104 - Abdullah ibn Shabib and Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, he said: I witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I had but one hair - then Allah increased me in beards afterwards. These words, we do not know anyone who narrated them except Sa'd; and we do not know them narrated from Sa'd with this wording except through this channel. And his saying: ""I had but one hair"" means: I had but one daughter; then Allah increased of beards - meaning: of children."
"1124","1105 - Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to bring him news of a people. So I went, running, until I reached the people; then I came back, walking calmly, until I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he asked me, and I told him. So he said: ""You went swiftly, then came back calmly"" - or as he said. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I disliked running, lest the people think I had fled. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sa'd is indeed experienced."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Sa'd; and we do not know for it a chain from Sa'd except this chain."
"1125","1106 - Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ""looked at Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas and deemed him small when he went out to Badr, then permitted him."" Sa'd said: So it is said he dragged his sword. Abdullah said: He was killed on the day of Badr. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1126","1107 - Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined; I broke fast in the month of Ramadan deliberately. He said: ""Free a neck."" He said: I do not find. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I am not able. He said: Then feed sixty poor. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it except al-Waqidi; and al-Waqidi - the people of knowledge have spoken about him."
"1127","Among what Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd narrated from his father, from his grandfather. 1108 - al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There was no prophet but that he described the Dajjal to his Ummah; and I shall describe him with a description no prophet before me described: he is blind in the right eye."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know Dawud narrating except this hadith without disagreement; and he narrated another hadith in which there is disagreement."
"1128","1109 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us with it, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Sa'd - thus Yahya ibn Ayyub said. And Ibn Lahi'ah said: from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If what a fingernail carries of what is in Paradise appeared to the people of the earth, what is between the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned for them. And if a man stretched out his hand and his bracelet appeared, its light would efface the light of the sun, as the sun effaces the stars - or: the light of the stars."""
"1129","Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather; and some of the companions of Abd al-Hamid said: from Dawud ibn Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When plague occurs in a land and you are in it, do not leave it; and when it occurs in a land and you are not in it, do not enter upon it."" 1110 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated it to us with it; and we left this hadith because of disagreement in it. And we do not know a son of Umar ibn Sa'd called Dawud."
"1130","Among what Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1111 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded placing the hands and erecting the feet in prayer. We do not know Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrating from Amir, from his father, except this hadith. And Wuhayb has been contradicted in this hadith from Ibn Ajlan; so others than Wuhayb narrated it from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah. Thus Yahya ibn Ayyub and Muhammad ibn az-Zibriqan narrated it. And some of the companions of Ibn Ajlan narrated it from Ibn Ajlan, from Sumayy, from an-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, mursal. And we do not know Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrating from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except this hadith."
"1131","Among what Muslim ibn A'idh narrated from Amir, from his father Sa'd. 1112 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muslim ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1132","1113 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd, that a man came to prayer while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying with us. When he reached the row he said: O Allah, give me the best You give Your righteous servants. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer he said: ""Who is the speaker just now?"" The man said: I. He said: ""Then your horse will be hamstrung, and you will be martyred in the path of Allah."" We do not know Muslim ibn A'idh, nor Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn A'idh, narrating from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except this hadith; and we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1133","Among what Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. 1114 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: Allah is Tayyib and loves what is tayyib; Clean and loves cleanliness; Generous and loves generosity; Bountiful and loves bounty. So clean your courtyards and open spaces, and do not resemble the Jews, who gather dunghills in their houses. Khalid said: So I mentioned that to Muhajir ibn Mismar, and he said: Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning similar to it - except that he said: ""Clean your courtyards."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1134","1115 - Abbas ibn Abdillah al-Baksasa'i narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Muhajir ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out to the Eid walking, and return walking, by a road other than the road by which he went out. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain. And this Khalid ibn Ilyas is not strong; and al-Muhajir ibn Mismar is a well-known man, sound in hadith; Hatim ibn Ismail and others narrated from him."
"1135","1116 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father, he said: Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid without adhan nor iqamah; and he would deliver two sermons standing, separating between them with a sitting. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1136","Among what Musa ibn Uqbah narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. 1117 - Umar ibn al-Khattab as-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Accept from the doers of good of the Ansar, and overlook their evildoers."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1137","1118 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: I would see the two sides of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to his right and to his left, when he greeted. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Musa ibn Uqbah, from Amir, except from the narration of Abu Ma'shar, from him."
"1138","Among what Abu Hazim narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. 1119 - Umar ibn Hafs ash-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abu Sakhr narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd - and I think him Amir - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Islam began strange, and it shall return as it began; so glad tidings to the strangers."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1139","Among what Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated from Amir, from his father Sa'd. 1120 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir ibn Sa'd narrating, he said: A man said to Sa'd: What prevents you from reviling Ali? He said: I shall not revile him as long as I remember three things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him; that one of them had been said to me would be more beloved to me than red camels. So a man said to him: What are they, O Abu Ishaq? He said: I shall not revile him as long as I remember when revelation came down upon him, and he covered him, and his daughter Fatimah, and his two sons, and brought them under his garment, then said: ""O Allah, these are my family and the people of my house."" And I shall not revile him when he left him behind in a raid he raided; so Ali said to him: You have left me behind with the women and children. So he said to him: ""Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophethood after me."" And I shall not revile him as long as I remember the day of Khaybar, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man whom Allah and His Messenger love; Allah shall conquer at his hands."" So people craned for it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Where is Ali?"" They said: There he is. He said: ""Call him."" So they called him, and he spat in his eye, then gave him the banner; so Allah conquered upon him. He said: So by Allah, that man did not mention him with a letter until he left Madinah. This hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Bukayr ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1140","1121 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from his father, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged the child to the bed (firash). This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1141","1122 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam captured al-Walid ibn al-Walid on the day of Badr; so Hisham ibn al-Walid came to ransom him. So I gave him my right, and al-Zubayr took his right of the ransom. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1142","1123 - Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Sulayman az-Zayyat, a man of the people of Iraq, narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In the Fire there is a stone called Wayl; the notables ascend upon it and descend in it."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Sa'd with this chain."
"1143","Uthman ibn Hakim from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1124 - Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn Khuza'i, of the offspring of Abdullah ibn al-Mu'qil, narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No one endures the hardship of Madinah except that I shall be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through more than this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except Uthman ibn Hakim. And a group narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1144","1125 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we passed by the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and prayed two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him. Then he supplicated his Lord long, then said: ""I asked my Lord three things: I asked Him not to destroy my Ummah by famine, and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to destroy them by drowning, and He gave it to me; and I asked Him not to make their violence among them, and He withheld it from me."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir except Uthman ibn Hakim; and we do not know Uthman ibn Hakim narrating from Amir except these two hadiths. And a group narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, and Anas ibn Malik, and Khalid Abu Nafi' ibn Khalid, and a group."
"1145","Among what Ishaq ibn Salim narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1126 - Ismail ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: my father Ishaq ibn Salim narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that he rode to his palace at al-Aqiq, and found a slave-boy cutting a tree, so he stripped him. When Sa'd returned, the people of the slave came asking him to return to them what he had taken from their slave-boy. So he said: ""Allah forbid that I return anything the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me as spoils"" - and he refused to return it to them. This hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Sa'd; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except Amir. And Ishaq ibn Salim narrated it from Amir, as did Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd."
"1146","Among what Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Atiq narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father Sa'd. 1127 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Atiq narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""When one of you spits, let him bury his spittle, lest it touch the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir ibn Sa'd except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Atiq."
"1147","Among what Abu Waqid - and his name is Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah - narrated from Amir, from his father Sa'd. 1128 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abu Waqid, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The hand is cut for a quarter dinar."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Amir except Abu Waqid. And this Abu Waqid - Wuhayb and Hatim and others than them narrated from him."
"1148","Among what al-Hasan ibn Uthman narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father - and he is of the offspring of Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf. 1129 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, of the offspring of Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, from al-Hasan ibn Uthman, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believer is atoned (mukaffar)."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd; and we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
"1149","Among what al-Hakim ibn Abdillah ibn Qays narrated from Amir, from his father. 1130 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Abdillah ibn Qays narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever says when he hears the mu'adhdhin: And I testify that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; I am pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Muhammad as Messenger, and with Islam as religion - his sin is forgiven."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this chain."
"1150","Among what Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Aswad narrated from Amir, from his father. 1131 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Sa'd, he said: Sa'd said - and he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he said: I saw him on the day of the Trench laughing until his molars appeared. He said: I said: How? He said: There was a man with a shield, and Sa'd was a marksman. So he would say thus and thus with the shield, covering his forehead. So Sa'd drew for him with an arrow; when he raised his head, he shot him, and it did not miss this of him - meaning his forehead - and he turned over, and raised his leg. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared. He said: I said: At what did he laugh? He said: At the deed of the man. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; nor was these words narrated connected; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Sa'd; and we do not know for it a path from Sa'd except this path."
"1151","Among what Yahya ibn an-Nadr and Abu al-Aswad narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1132 - Muhammad ibn al-Haytham ibn Ubaydillah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, and Yahya ibn an-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, spare them whoever besets them with violence"" - meaning the people of Madinah - ""and no one intends it (Madinah) with evil except that Allah melts him as salt melts in water."" We do not know Abu al-Aswad and Yahya ibn an-Nadr narrating from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, except this hadith."
"1152","Among what Hashim ibn Hashim narrated from Amir, from his father. 1133 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats in the morning in a day seven dates, no poison shall harm him that day."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hashim ibn Hashim. And there has been disagreement over Hashim ibn Hashim: some narrated it from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father; and some narrated it from Hashim ibn Hashim, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father. And some narrated it from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Sa'd - so he erred in it, for we do not know Sa'd to have a son called Khalid."
"1153","1134 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at an-Nabawiyyah - or: at an-Naba'ah - saying: ""Soon you shall distinguish the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire."" They said: O Messenger of Allah, by what? He said: ""By good praise, and bad praise."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'd except Amir; nor from Amir except Hashim ibn Hashim; nor from Hashim ibn Hashim except Shuja'; and we heard it only from al-Hasan ibn Arafah."
"1154","1135 - Muhammad ibn Isa at-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Amiri, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening (awda'a) in the valley of Muhassir. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by other than Sa'd; and we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain. And this Abu Bakr is Abu Bakr ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Sabrah, and he is lenient in hadith."
"1155","1136 - Raja ibn Abdur-Rahman, a Baghdadi, narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Hashim ibn Hashim, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: I fell ill in Makkah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah that He not turn me back upon my heel. He said: So he said: ""Perhaps Allah shall raise you"" - meaning: cure you of your illness - ""so peoples benefit by you."" He said: I said: I wish to bequeath, and I have only a daughter. I said: Shall I bequeath half? He said: Half is much. I said: Then a third? He said: A third; and a third is much - or: great - Zakariyya doubted. He said: So people bequeathed a third, and that was permitted. This hadith, we know it not from the hadith of Hashim ibn Hashim, from Amir, from his father, except from the hadith of Marwan."
"1156","Among what Bijad ibn Musa narrated from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father. 1137 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Abi Muhammad narrated to us, from Bijad ibn Musa, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a handspan of land without its right shall be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths; and neither sarf nor adl shall be accepted from him. And whoever claims (lineage) to other than his father, or to other than his patrons, has disbelieved."" Abu Bakr said: Meaning: the favour (ni'mah). This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd with this wording and the completion of these words except through this channel with this chain."
"1157","Among what Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated from his father Sa'd. 1138 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad az-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I marvel at the believer: he is rewarded in all his affair. If good befalls him, he praises Allah and is rewarded; and if a calamity befalls him, he praises Allah and is rewarded. So he is rewarded in all his affair, even the morsel he raises to the mouth of his wife."" This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through more than one channel; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad. And it is only known from the hadith of Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1158","1139 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The believer is imprinted upon every trait except treachery and lying."" This hadith is narrated from Sa'd through more than one channel, mawquf; and we do not know anyone who raised it (marfu') except Ali ibn Hashim, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, with this chain."
"1159","1140 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza when the covenant was near. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza when the covenant was near. So he said: ""You have said something vile (hujr). Spit - or: blow - to your left three times; and seek refuge with Allah from Satan; and seek forgiveness from Allah; and do not return."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Sa'd except through this channel, from the narration of Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father. And we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a sound channel sounder than this channel."
"1160","Among what Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated from Mus'ab, from his father. 1141 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1161","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1162","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa told us, from Shayban, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd and Amr ibn Maymun, from Sa'd."
"1163","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd — their narrations being close to one another — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the most decrepit age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave"" — or ""from the punishment of the grave."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel, and it is the most authentic of what is narrated from Sa'd."
"1164","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Hassan told us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {Those who are heedless of their prayer} — and he said: ""They are those who delay it past its time."" This hadith has been narrated by the trustworthy memorizers from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, as mawquf (attributed to Sa'd, not raised to the Prophet), and we do not know anyone who raised it (to the Prophet) except Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr — and Ikrimah is weak in hadith."
"1165","Hatim ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Hammad told us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, in a raised (marfu') report, he said: ""Stick to archery, for it is the best — or among the best — of your pastimes."" This hadith is, according to the trustworthy narrators, mawquf (stopped at Sa'd), and we have not heard of anyone raising it except Hatim, from Yahya ibn Hammad, from Abu Awanah."
"1166","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr told us, saying: Za'idah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me in my illness, and I said: Shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: ""No."" I said: Half? He said: ""No."" I said: Then a third? And he said: ""A third — and a third is much."""
"1167","And Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated it to us, saying: Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur told us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr told us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"1168","Among what Simak ibn Harb narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, saying: Simak told us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: Four verses were revealed concerning me: I came by a sword, so I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come by a sword — and this verse was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils of war; say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger}. And a man prepared food and invited us, and we drank wine until we became intoxicated, and the Ansar and Quraysh boasted against one another: the Ansar said, ""We are better,"" and Quraysh said, ""We are better"" — so a man among them stood up and struck his nose, and Sa'd's nose was the one struck — and this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are but filth from the work of Satan, so avoid it} — the verse. He said: And my mother said: Do you not claim that Allah commands you to uphold kinship and to be dutiful to parents? By Allah, I shall neither eat food nor drink drink until you disbelieve — and she neither ate food nor drank drink, and when they wanted to feed her they would pry open her mouth with a stick and get food and drink into it — so this verse was revealed: {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents, but if they strive with you to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them}. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me when I was ill, and I said: Shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: ""No."" I said: Half? And he forbade me. I said: A third? And he remained silent — and the people adopted it. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the narration of Sa'd, and we do not know for it from Sa'd any chain except this chain with this wording."
"1169","Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ishaq told us, saying: Sharik told us, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people most severely afflicted are the prophets, then the best, then the best."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Simak except Sharik, and it is only known from the hadith of Asim, from Mus'ab."
"1170","Among what al-Suddi narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn al-Mufaddal told us, saying: Asbat ibn Nasr told us, saying: al-Suddi claimed, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to the people except four men and two women, and he said: ""Kill them even if you find them clinging to the coverings of the Ka'bah: Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, Abdullah ibn Khatal, Miqyas ibn Subabah, and Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi al-Sarh."" As for Abdullah ibn Khatal, he was caught while clinging to the coverings of the Ka'bah, and Sa'd and Ammar raced toward him, so Sa'd outran Ammar and killed him. As for Miqyas ibn Subabah, the people caught up with him in the marketplace and killed him. As for Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, he boarded the sea and a violent storm struck them, so the people of the ship said: ""Be sincere, for your gods avail you nothing"" — so Ikrimah said: ""If nothing but sincerity will save me at sea, nothing but it will save me on land. O Allah, I make a covenant to You: if You deliver me from what I am in, I shall surely come to Muhammad until I place my hand in his hand."" He said: So he accepted Islam. He said: As for Abdullah ibn Abi al-Sarh, Uthman shielded him, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to give the pledge, he brought him and stood him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept the pledge of Abdullah — and he raised his head looking at him, each time refusing — then he accepted his pledge after three times. Then he turned and praised Allah and glorified Him and said: ""Was there not among you a right-minded man who, when he saw me withholding my hand from his pledge, would kill him?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you had gestured to us with your eyes! He said: ""It is not fitting for a prophet that he should have treacherous glances."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except from Sa'd, with this chain."
"1171","Among what Amr ibn Murrah narrated from Mus'ab from his father: al-Husayn ibn Amr al-Anqazi narrated to us, saying: My father told me. And al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad ibn Hafs narrated to us — both saying: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi told us, saying: Khallad ibn Muslim told us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, concerning the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you might understand. We relate to you the best of stories} — the verse. He said: So the Qur'an came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited it to them for a time, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you would relate stories to us! So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you might understand. We relate to you the best of stories}. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you would narrate traditions to us! So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Allah has sent down the best of speech, a consistent Book}. Each time, they were commanded with the Qur'an, or disciplined by the Qur'an. Khallad said: And he added to me therein: They said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you would remind us! So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Has the time not come for those who believe that their hearts should become humble at the remembrance of Allah}. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd with this chain, nor do we know anyone to have narrated it from Sa'd except Mus'ab, nor from Mus'ab except Amr ibn Murrah, nor from Amr ibn Murrah except Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, nor from Amr ibn Qays except Khallad ibn Muslim."
"1172","Among what Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd told us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely afflicted? He said: ""The prophets, then the best, then the best. The servant is tried according to his religion: if he is firm, his trial is intensified, and if there is softness in his religion, he is tried according to that measure. Tribulations do not cease with the servant until they leave him walking upon the earth with no sin upon him."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated except from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Sa'd with this wording except Mus'ab. And this hadith has been narrated from Asim by a group, among them Hammad, al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, Hisham the companion of al-Dastuwai, and others."
"1173","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: al-Muharibi told us, saying: al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab told us, from Asim, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1174","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah told us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl containing tharid, and they ate from it, and some remained over. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man of Paradise shall eat this leftover"" — or ""that leftover."" And I had left my brother Umayr at home, so I hoped it would be him — then Abdullah ibn Salam came and ate it. This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd except Asim ibn Bahdalah, and it has been narrated from Asim by more than one."
"1175","Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Nabhan told us, saying: Asim told us, from Mus'ab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of you is he who learns the Qur'an and teaches it."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Asim, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, except al-Harith ibn Nabhan. And Sharik has contradicted al-Harith ibn Nabhan in the chain of this hadith: Sharik narrated it from Asim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. And al-Harith is not a memorizer, and Sharik takes precedence over him in the view of the people of hadith, even though he too is not a memorizer."
"1176","Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Nabhan told us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: {Alif Lam Mim. The revelation} and {Has there come upon man}. This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And al-Harith ibn Nabhan — our remark about him has already preceded. And al-Husayn ibn Waqid and Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan have contradicted him, narrating it from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah — and in my view that is the correct one."
"1177","Among what Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath told us, saying: My father told me, saying: Mis'ar told us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: I used to think I had merit over those behind me — or he used to think he had merit over those behind him — until he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""You are only granted victory through your weak ones."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mus'ab, but they differed in raising it: some of them said, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mus'ab, that Sa'd said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... and Muhammad ibn Talhah said, from his father, from Mus'ab, from his father. And we do not know anyone to have narrated this hadith from Mis'ar, connected, from Talhah, with this chain, except Hafs ibn Ghiyath, nor from Hafs except Umar. And something like these words has also been narrated from Abu al-Darda'."
"1178","Among what Musa al-Juhani narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan told us, saying: Musa al-Juhani told us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day?"" A questioner among his companions asked him: O Messenger of Allah, how can one of us earn a thousand good deeds? He said: ""He glorifies Allah a hundred times, so a thousand good deeds are written for him, or a thousand sins are wiped away from him."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel, and none narrated it from Mus'ab except Musa al-Juhani. And it has been narrated from Musa by more than one. And we do not know these words to be narrated from anyone except from Sa'd, though something like it with different wording is narrated through other channels — we shall mention each wording of a hadith in its place with its chain."
"1179","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, saying: Musa al-Juhani told us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me words to say. He said: ""Say: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; and Allah is Most Great, abundantly; and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Most High, the Most Great"" — five. He said: These are for my Lord, so what is for me? He said: ""Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, guide me, and grant me well-being."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of Sa'd, nor did anyone narrate it from Sa'd except Mus'ab, nor from Mus'ab except Musa al-Juhani."
"1180","Al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ja'far al-Ahmar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Talhah told us, saying: Mindal told us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever claims (descent) from other than his father while knowing his father, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him."" This hadith has been narrated from Sa'd through other channels, but we do not know it to be narrated from the hadith of Mus'ab, from his father, except through this channel."
"1181","Among what al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father: Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar told us, saying: Kathir ibn Zayd told us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun (Jonah). He said: And a Bedouin came and distracted him, so I followed him, and he turned to me and said: ""Abu Ishaq?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""What is it?"" I said: You mentioned the supplication of Dhu al-Nun. Then a Bedouin came and distracted you. He said: ""Yes. The supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he called out in the belly of the whale: {There is no god but You; glory be to You; indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers} — for no one ever supplicates with it but he is answered."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Sa'd, from him. And it has been narrated from Sa'd through another channel. And this hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Kathir ibn Zayd except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, and al-Muttalib narrated from his father only this hadith."
"1182","Among what al-Zubayr ibn Adi narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, saying: al-Zubayr ibn Adi told us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: I prayed with my father and placed my hand like this — Yahya placed his two hands between his knees — so my father said: We used to do this, then we were commanded to raise (the hands) to the knees. This hadith has also been narrated by Abu Ishaq from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"1183","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa told us, saying: Isra'il told us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Mus'ab, from his father, with the like thereof."
"1184","What Qanan ibn Abdullah al-Nahmi narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah told us, saying: Qanan ibn Abdullah told us, from Mus'ab, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever harms Ali has harmed me."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1185","Among what Abu Sa'id al-A'sam narrated from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath told us, from his father, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Sa'id al-A'sam, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man loudly seeking his lost item in the mosque and said: ""May you not find it."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except with this chain."
"1186","Among what an unnamed man of Banu Amir narrated from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir told us, saying: al-Mughirah told us, from a man of Banu Amir, saying: Mus'ab ibn Sa'd told us, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I fear for you the trial of prosperity more than the trial of adversity. You have been tried with the trial of adversity and you were patient; and indeed, this world is sweet and green."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel with this chain."
"1187","What Abu Balj narrated from Mus'ab from his father: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Abu Balj, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Close off from me every small door into the mosque except the small door of Ali."" This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels, but we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this route. And I think Mu'alla erred in it, because Shu'bah and Abu Awanah narrate it from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas — and that is the correct one."
"1188","What al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated from Mus'ab: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from al-Hakam, from Mus'ab, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: ""Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me?"" This hadith has been narrated by Shu'bah from al-Hakam, from Mus'ab, from his father — and that is the correct one. And Layth narrated it from al-Hakam, from A'ishah bint Sa'd, from her father — while the hadith of Shu'bah from al-Hakam is the correct one."
"1189","Among what Abu Ishaq narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Abu al-Hasan al-Samut narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar told us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad told us, saying: Isra'il told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except from Muhammad, from his father. And it has been narrated from others besides Sa'd through various channels, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ibn Umar, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Mas'ud, Abu Ayyub, and Anas narrated it — so we mentioned it from Sa'd since it was sound, and he was the highest from whom it is narrated."
"1190","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Amr ibn Thabit told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."" This hadith, we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Sa'd except his son Muhammad, nor from Muhammad except Abu Ishaq."
"1191","Among what Yunus ibn Jubayr narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, saying: Shu'bah told us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except from the hadith of his son Muhammad, from his father. And we do not recall anyone to have narrated it from Muhammad except Yunus ibn Jubayr. And it has been narrated from others besides Sa'd: it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah and from Abu Sa'id — while Sa'd was the highest to narrate it, so we mentioned it from Sa'd. And we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except with this chain."
"1192","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Minhal told us, saying: Hammam told us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth? He said: ""No."" He said: Half? He said: ""No."" He said: A third? He said: ""A third — and a third is much"" — then he mentioned the hadith."
"1193","Among what Yusuf ibn al-Hakam narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd told us, saying: My father told me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan, from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, except through this channel. And it has also been narrated from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — meaning, whoever humiliates Quraysh."
"1194","Among what Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from his father, from his grandfather: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to announce on the days of Tashriq: ""They are days of eating and drinking."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel, with this chain."
"1195","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd. And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, saying: Abu Amir told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd told us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the happiness of a man is his seeking good from his Lord and his contentment with what He decrees; and among the wretchedness of a man is his abandoning seeking good (istikhara) and his displeasure after the decree."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated with this wording except from Sa'd. And we do not know anyone to have narrated it from Sa'd except his son Muhammad. And it was narrated from Isma'il by Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr."
"1196","As for the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, saying: Umar ibn Ali told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, a man of Quraysh, told us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like thereof."
"1197","Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Fadl al-Allaf narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd told us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three are part of happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious dwelling, and a comfortable mount."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel, from Sa'd. And this Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd is not strong, though a group of scholars have narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"1198","Among what Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Kurdi narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah told us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid told us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1199","And Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated it to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bishr told us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid told us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The month is like this and like this"" — and he withheld a finger on the third (gesture). And it has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels, while the highest to narrate this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Sa'd, with this chain. Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel. And it has been narrated by more than one from Isma'il, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, as mursal; while a group raised it (to the Prophet with full chain), among them Za'idah, Muhammad ibn Bishr, and Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah."
"1200","Among what Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya narrated from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Iyad told us, saying: My uncle Utaybah told me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So-and-so al-Thaqafi has been killed, and he had accepted Islam — so he said: ""May Allah cast him far away; he used to hate Quraysh."" This hadith, we do not know it to be narrated from Sa'd except through this channel."
